WEBVTT

1
00:01:58.743 --> 00:02:00.620
[door opens]

2
00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:02.706
[woman]
Andy, is that you?

3
00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.457
[door closes]

4
00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:07.960
[woman]
Oh, hi, Zeke. Did you hear anything?

5
00:02:08.044 --> 00:02:09.503
[Zeke]
Not yet, no.

6
00:02:16.719 --> 00:02:19.639
- [Zeke] Morning, Sally.
- Morning.

7
00:02:19.723 --> 00:02:23.852
[woman] You hungry? Run downstairs
and grab a box of cereal.

8
00:02:23.935 --> 00:02:25.353
[exhales]

9
00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.659
Hey. Shh!

10
00:02:39.742 --> 00:02:42.329
Hey, it's just me. It's just me. Hi.

11
00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:44.789
Did you come down
to get some Fruit Loops?

12
00:02:44.872 --> 00:02:47.250
Okay, okay. Shh!

13
00:02:48.377 --> 00:02:50.170
Here you go.

14
00:02:52.129 --> 00:02:55.509
There you go.
Okay, now can you do something for me?

15
00:02:56.468 --> 00:02:57.676
When you go back upstairs,

16
00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.764
don't tell anybody
that you saw Daddy down here, okay?

17
00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.808
All right, it'll be our little secret.
Won't that be fun?

18
00:03:03.891 --> 00:03:06.228
To have just a little secret
between the two of us?

19
00:03:06.311 --> 00:03:08.562
All right? Okay, so remember. Now, shh!

20
00:03:08.646 --> 00:03:10.064
Shh.

21
00:03:14.985 --> 00:03:16.737
[stairs creaking]

22
00:03:28.332 --> 00:03:29.835
Thank you, Uncle Zeke.

23
00:03:30.961 --> 00:03:34.463
Sally, were you speaking to someone
down in the basement?

24
00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.216
No.

25
00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.885
Sally has an imaginary friend
named Melissa.

26
00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:43.973
[phone ringing]

27
00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:48.728
Hello? Oh, hi, Reed.

28
00:03:48.812 --> 00:03:50.438
Any word about Andy?

29
00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.150
Hang on.

30
00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:58.530
Mornin'.

31
00:04:01.366 --> 00:04:03.159
He's not answering his phone?

32
00:04:04.161 --> 00:04:06.621
Well, you better tell the Feds
to meet us there.

33
00:04:06.705 --> 00:04:08.372
[footsteps departing]

34
00:04:08.456 --> 00:04:10.834
Sally Ann, where do you think
you're going?

35
00:04:13.336 --> 00:04:15.629
Oh, yeah, you bet. I'll see you in a few.

36
00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.341
[footsteps approaching]

37
00:04:22.012 --> 00:04:24.764
Sally! Go upstairs.

38
00:04:24.848 --> 00:04:28.268
- But I want...
- Go upstairs now.

39
00:04:29.351 --> 00:04:30.394
[bowl clatters]

40
00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:52.542
[tires screeching]

41
00:04:54.668 --> 00:04:57.379
[tires screeching, vehicle departing]

42
00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:03.512
Ezekiel! It's the damnedest thing.
Someone just stole my car!

43
00:05:04.471 --> 00:05:06.430
- You don't say?
- It's an '87 Cavalier.

44
00:05:06.514 --> 00:05:07.807
You should be more surprised.

45
00:05:09.391 --> 00:05:12.896
- [sighs] Surprise is for the ill-prepared.
- What?

46
00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:16.233
Want a ride to work?

47
00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:18.944
Hey, baby, it's me.
[chuckles]

48
00:05:19.026 --> 00:05:22.572
Hey, I fucking got it.
When can you get away?

49
00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:28.577
Okay, Shimmer Lake?
I'll wait for you. Okay.

50
00:05:41.091 --> 00:05:42.259
Fuck, Zeke.

51
00:05:43.552 --> 00:05:44.636
Mornin', Harris.

52
00:05:44.718 --> 00:05:47.721
Guess you're ridin' up front, huh?
Is that right, Zeke? Good.

53
00:05:49.014 --> 00:05:51.768
Why?

54
00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.144
[grunts]

55
00:05:58.899 --> 00:06:01.944
- Morning, Reed. Everything all right?
- Yeah, everything's just peachy.

56
00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:03.028
[starts engine]

57
00:06:05.072 --> 00:06:08.285
- How's the shoulder?
- It hurts.

58
00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:09.952
Ask a stupid question.

59
00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:15.040
Actually, when the bullet hit me,
it didn't hurt as much as you'd think.

60
00:06:16.084 --> 00:06:18.295
Well, you're a tougher man than I am.

61
00:06:21.798 --> 00:06:24.009
- Thanks for the ride.
- Don't mention it.

62
00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:32.266
You know, I'm up for good-natured ribbing
between partners and everything,

63
00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:35.728
but when you do it in front of someone,
it makes the other person feel weird.

64
00:06:35.812 --> 00:06:38.773
He didn't know where to sit at first,
and it was like... [sighs]

65
00:07:16.185 --> 00:07:17.937
Think I could've been FBI?

66
00:07:18.021 --> 00:07:20.314
Couldn't do any worse than these assholes.

67
00:07:20.398 --> 00:07:23.108
Yeah. Thanks, man.

68
00:07:24.069 --> 00:07:26.153
Did you see anything
at the Burton place last night?

69
00:07:26.237 --> 00:07:28.197
Nothing but phantom naked school boys.

70
00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:32.117
I swear to God I saw a naked kid
trotting from one yard to the next.

71
00:07:32.201 --> 00:07:34.788
Right. Other than that, nothin'.
Nobody came, nobody left.

72
00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:36.538
Closed the bedroom curtains around ten.

73
00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:38.707
- Regrettably.
- Lights went off at eleven.

74
00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:40.752
Why regrettably on the curtains?

75
00:07:40.834 --> 00:07:42.312
- Well, you know...
- She's smokin' hot.

76
00:07:42.336 --> 00:07:44.673
She's smokin' fuckin' hot. That's why.

77
00:07:44.755 --> 00:07:47.466
- Hey, where is she from in Mexico?
- Why would that matter?

78
00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:50.595
Well, I think we'd probably want
to vacation down there.

79
00:07:52.514 --> 00:07:54.223
Seriously, though, I did see a naked kid.

80
00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:57.435
- Jesus. Enough already, will ya?
- I just... I saw it.

81
00:07:57.519 --> 00:07:58.788
- You represent the Bureau.
- [knocking]

82
00:07:58.812 --> 00:08:01.355
[Zeke]
Judge Dawkins? Can you open up, please?

83
00:08:01.439 --> 00:08:03.483
Why do we care
this Dawkins guy went AWOL?

84
00:08:03.565 --> 00:08:06.110
- Well, the bank was robbed on Tuesday.
- [doorbell ringing]

85
00:08:06.194 --> 00:08:07.278
Dawkins owns it.

86
00:08:07.362 --> 00:08:09.697
So they robbed the bank,
came back, stole the banker?

87
00:08:09.781 --> 00:08:12.283
Well, maybe Dawkins
was involved in the robbery.

88
00:08:12.367 --> 00:08:14.786
Why would a guy who owns a bank
need money?

89
00:08:14.869 --> 00:08:19.374
That is an excellent question.
Do they teach you that at Quantico?

90
00:08:19.456 --> 00:08:21.250
- [chuckles]
- Mm.

91
00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:23.752
- Rippin' on you.
- Yeah, you think so?

92
00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:27.173
Judge Dawkins! Zeke Sikes!
Can you open up, please?

93
00:08:29.341 --> 00:08:30.343
Oh.

94
00:08:34.639 --> 00:08:36.182
Judge?

95
00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:47.360
[phone ringing]

96
00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:51.155
Sikes. Martha?
This is really not a good...

97
00:08:52.282 --> 00:08:54.743
Yes, I will let you know as soon as...

98
00:08:56.619 --> 00:08:57.953
All right, look forward to it.

99
00:08:59.998 --> 00:09:03.333
- Martha's making meat loaf.
- Task at hand, huh?

100
00:09:03.418 --> 00:09:05.961
- I fucking hate meat loaf.
- [Reed exhales]

101
00:09:09.631 --> 00:09:10.631
[whistling]

102
00:09:12.594 --> 00:09:13.720
Better get 'em out.

103
00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:24.605
Judge?

104
00:10:19.244 --> 00:10:20.912
[footsteps]

105
00:10:20.995 --> 00:10:22.663
[vehicle door closes]

106
00:11:03.495 --> 00:11:07.583
[printer whirring]

107
00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:10.461
[Zeke]
How many times do I have to tell you guys?

108
00:11:10.544 --> 00:11:12.547
Ed is the guy we're looking for.

109
00:11:12.629 --> 00:11:14.465
Andy is just a patsy.

110
00:11:14.548 --> 00:11:17.719
We understand that you got
strong feelings on the matter.

111
00:11:17.802 --> 00:11:21.889
The son of a bitch
looked me in the eyes and shot me.

112
00:11:21.972 --> 00:11:24.475
- That's not feelings. That's fact.
- Oh, come on, Zeke.

113
00:11:24.558 --> 00:11:27.061
This is where Kyle and I can
use the Bureau's resources

114
00:11:27.144 --> 00:11:30.023
to help you catch these guys
before they vanish into thin air.

115
00:11:30.105 --> 00:11:32.942
We're expanding the net
to a ten-state radius,

116
00:11:33.025 --> 00:11:36.278
we got APBs out
to every government agency,

117
00:11:36.361 --> 00:11:39.615
and we got checkpoints
on every major highway

118
00:11:39.698 --> 00:11:42.201
in every direction for 300 miles.

119
00:11:43.119 --> 00:11:45.078
- You done?
- Yes, he is.

120
00:11:45.163 --> 00:11:47.498
But that was a lot of stuff.

121
00:11:47.581 --> 00:11:51.543
- What if they're still here?
- Why would they still be here?

122
00:11:51.628 --> 00:11:54.463
Ed told his wife he's got
one more thing to take care of.

123
00:11:54.547 --> 00:11:57.884
- Dawkins was that thing.
- What about Andy?

124
00:11:57.966 --> 00:11:59.677
Andy's with Ed.

125
00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:02.429
We got two sets of footprints
coming out of the Dawkins house...

126
00:12:02.513 --> 00:12:04.599
And they were going off
in different directions.

127
00:12:04.682 --> 00:12:07.434
All right. So what? So maybe
they chopped the money then and there,

128
00:12:07.518 --> 00:12:08.879
and then went their separate ways.

129
00:12:08.937 --> 00:12:11.022
Or maybe they left two trails
to confuse us.

130
00:12:11.105 --> 00:12:12.731
I don't even see how it matters.

131
00:12:12.815 --> 00:12:14.232
Well, you'll see that it matters

132
00:12:14.317 --> 00:12:17.736
when we find my brother Andy's dead body,
you stupid assholes.

133
00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:18.820
Oh!

134
00:12:21.407 --> 00:12:24.243
Your partner's being
real pig-headed about this.

135
00:12:24.326 --> 00:12:26.412
My partner?

136
00:12:26.495 --> 00:12:28.831
My partner's the smartest guy in the room,

137
00:12:28.914 --> 00:12:31.625
and if you don't see that,
you two are dumber than you look.

138
00:12:37.005 --> 00:12:40.677
His partner's not even in the room.
I don't even... I don't...

139
00:12:40.759 --> 00:12:42.470
I don't see how that makes any sense.

140
00:12:43.471 --> 00:12:44.639
[tapping]

141
00:12:44.721 --> 00:12:46.515
- Hey.
- I'm not stranding you, am I?

142
00:12:46.599 --> 00:12:49.038
No, no. I'll hitch a ride
with Beavis and Butthead back there.

143
00:12:49.101 --> 00:12:50.394
Where you going?

144
00:12:50.477 --> 00:12:52.480
Oh, I thought I'd swing
past the Burton place

145
00:12:52.562 --> 00:12:55.482
just to see if Ed thinks twice
about leaving Steph behind.

146
00:12:55.566 --> 00:12:59.903
Plus, maybe if I stay there long enough,
I can avoid Martha's dinner.

147
00:12:59.988 --> 00:13:02.365
- Can you do me a favor?
- Yeah.

148
00:13:02.447 --> 00:13:04.366
Just keep an eye on those two.

149
00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.535
They seem like decent guys.

150
00:13:06.619 --> 00:13:08.495
I just...

151
00:13:08.578 --> 00:13:12.291
If Andy turns up,
I'd rather hear about it first

152
00:13:12.375 --> 00:13:13.625
before he gets gunned down.

153
00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:15.628
You really think Andy's still here?

154
00:13:17.713 --> 00:13:19.506
He was at the house last night.

155
00:13:20.466 --> 00:13:22.466
Any information I get,
you'll be the first to know.

156
00:13:23.427 --> 00:13:24.428
Thanks, partner.

157
00:13:42.447 --> 00:13:44.907
[curtains rattling]

158
00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:46.616
[laughing]

159
00:13:46.701 --> 00:13:49.245
[both laughing]

160
00:13:50.163 --> 00:13:51.456
How about this?

161
00:13:52.414 --> 00:13:54.625
There's a woman
who looks exactly like Steph Burton,

162
00:13:54.709 --> 00:13:56.711
except she's three feet tall.

163
00:13:56.793 --> 00:13:57.879
Yes or no?

164
00:13:58.546 --> 00:13:59.922
- [mumbles]
- [radio static]

165
00:14:00.005 --> 00:14:03.176
[man on radio] <i>Agents Biltmore, Walker,</i>
<i>I think we have your suspects.</i>

166
00:14:04.634 --> 00:14:05.845
This is Biltmore.

167
00:14:07.138 --> 00:14:09.599
Yeah. Yeah, that could...

168
00:14:09.682 --> 00:14:11.142
Wait, say that again?

169
00:14:12.601 --> 00:14:14.227
No. No, no, no, no, no.

170
00:14:14.312 --> 00:14:16.980
The Camaro is black
and the suspects are white.

171
00:14:18.274 --> 00:14:21.985
[sighs] No, you should...
You should definitely cut them loose.

172
00:14:23.696 --> 00:14:26.698
Yeah, I agree. That is...
It's quite the coincidence, right?

173
00:14:26.783 --> 00:14:29.701
But, no, you should let them go.

174
00:14:29.786 --> 00:14:33.121
I'm sure of it. Thank you.

175
00:14:41.254 --> 00:14:43.966
- Hey, babe.
- Pop the trunk!

176
00:14:44.049 --> 00:14:46.302
Hey, what took you so long?

177
00:14:46.385 --> 00:14:50.847
Zeke. He parked outside the house
for hours. I had to wait.

178
00:14:50.932 --> 00:14:53.142
That's my girl. Always thinking.

179
00:14:53.225 --> 00:14:55.311
Hey, I don't know about you,
but I'm starvin'.

180
00:14:55.394 --> 00:14:56.812
What do you say we stop...?

181
00:14:56.895 --> 00:14:59.356
[gasps]
No, please don't!

182
00:15:15.038 --> 00:15:16.666
[clock ticking]

183
00:15:21.504 --> 00:15:23.380
[lighter clicking]

184
00:15:23.463 --> 00:15:28.260
[news theme music playing]

185
00:15:28.344 --> 00:15:30.554
[woman speaking indistinctly on TV]

186
00:15:35.143 --> 00:15:36.644
[line ringing]

187
00:15:38.855 --> 00:15:40.898
<i>This is Ed. Leave a message.
See what happens.</i>

188
00:15:40.981 --> 00:15:41.982
[machine beeps]

189
00:15:42.191 --> 00:15:43.692
Shit.

190
00:15:45.318 --> 00:15:47.738
[clock ticking]

191
00:15:53.702 --> 00:15:56.080
Stephanie? Steph?

192
00:15:57.248 --> 00:15:59.959
- Where the hell have you been?
- Where have I been?

193
00:16:00.042 --> 00:16:02.378
In a car, forever! The cornfield!

194
00:16:02.461 --> 00:16:04.797
I spent the night in a junkyard!

195
00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:07.091
Listen, Dawkins has the money.

196
00:16:08.049 --> 00:16:09.927
Dawkins?

197
00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:12.513
Shit. I should've known.

198
00:16:12.596 --> 00:16:16.767
- Why?
- Well, that's not important.

199
00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:19.479
What matters is, I gotta figure out
a way to get that money

200
00:16:19.562 --> 00:16:22.148
so we can get the hell out of here.

201
00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:23.941
What's to figure?

202
00:16:24.024 --> 00:16:25.025
Oh...

203
00:16:25.109 --> 00:16:28.403
What? You think Dawkins
is just gonna give you the money?

204
00:16:28.488 --> 00:16:31.865
Yeah, it's just...
I'm not much of a gun guy, Steph.

205
00:16:31.948 --> 00:16:33.951
- Become one.
- Jesus, Steph!

206
00:16:34.034 --> 00:16:35.786
- And go get that money.
- [sighs]

207
00:16:46.254 --> 00:16:47.298
[Martha]
Oh, please, Zeke.

208
00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:49.509
You can't start a day
on nothing but coffee.

209
00:16:49.591 --> 00:16:53.178
- Aren't you hungry?
- Um, not particularly, no.

210
00:16:53.261 --> 00:16:55.806
- You worried about your brother?
- That's it.

211
00:16:56.599 --> 00:16:59.434
- Well, isn't there anything you can do?
- Martha, I'm trying.

212
00:17:01.229 --> 00:17:04.523
I'm sorry. I'm just worried about him.

213
00:17:04.606 --> 00:17:07.067
I know Andy, and he just couldn't
do something like this.

214
00:17:07.151 --> 00:17:09.237
Martha, he's my brother and I love him,

215
00:17:09.319 --> 00:17:14.450
but, ultimately, it's gonna come down
to how bad he wants to save himself.

216
00:17:14.534 --> 00:17:16.368
What's that supposed to mean?

217
00:17:16.451 --> 00:17:18.954
Why are you crying, Mommy?

218
00:17:21.582 --> 00:17:23.375
I'm sorry, Martha.

219
00:17:23.459 --> 00:17:26.253
You and Sally deserve
better than this. I mean that.

220
00:17:26.336 --> 00:17:28.673
It never should have been this way.

221
00:17:28.756 --> 00:17:31.842
But I don't want to make promises
that I can't keep.

222
00:17:35.011 --> 00:17:38.348
Hey, Sally, what do you say
you and I take a ride in the cruiser?

223
00:17:39.224 --> 00:17:40.308
Really?

224
00:17:40.393 --> 00:17:43.563
I'm not asking people to be perfect, Sal.

225
00:17:43.645 --> 00:17:47.732
Everybody makes mistakes.
God knows I'm no exception.

226
00:17:48.858 --> 00:17:51.444
But everybody thinks that they can do
whatever the hell they want

227
00:17:51.528 --> 00:17:54.115
with no repercussions whatsoever.

228
00:17:54.656 --> 00:17:55.825
And what is the point

229
00:17:55.907 --> 00:17:59.494
of being the only clean person
in a town that's completely dirty?

230
00:17:59.578 --> 00:18:02.914
When I'm dirty, my mom gives me a bath.

231
00:18:04.375 --> 00:18:08.587
Yeah. Well... that's what I'm doing.

232
00:18:10.006 --> 00:18:12.842
- I'm giving this town a bath.
- Bath time!

233
00:18:12.924 --> 00:18:17.471
[siren wailing]

234
00:18:17.555 --> 00:18:21.017
- I thought you wasn't hungry.
- Oh, I'm starving.

235
00:18:21.099 --> 00:18:24.103
Then why didn't you eat
Mommy's breakfast?

236
00:18:24.185 --> 00:18:25.895
Because if I ate your mommy's breakfast,

237
00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:29.317
I'd end up a fat fucking bastard
like everybody else in this town.

238
00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:35.823
Let's just pretend Uncle Zeke
didn't say that, okay?

239
00:18:35.905 --> 00:18:38.742
- Okay.
- [footsteps approaching]

240
00:18:40.536 --> 00:18:41.703
Hey, Sally.

241
00:18:43.038 --> 00:18:46.083
Do you mind if we drop her off at school
on the way to work?

242
00:18:46.166 --> 00:18:47.960
No, not at all.

243
00:18:48.044 --> 00:18:50.837
Get in the back, you fat fuckin' bastard.

244
00:18:52.173 --> 00:18:54.467
- Excuse me?
- [chuckles]

245
00:18:54.549 --> 00:18:57.260
That's real nice. That's real nice.

246
00:18:57.345 --> 00:18:58.637
You're a nice little girl.

247
00:19:18.907 --> 00:19:24.913
[boy speaking indistinctly]

248
00:19:24.997 --> 00:19:27.540
[gun firing, glass breaking]

249
00:19:32.922 --> 00:19:37.050
- [clock ticking]
- [takes deep breath]

250
00:19:54.984 --> 00:19:57.278
You know,
I'm a police officer just like you.

251
00:19:57.363 --> 00:20:00.365
I may not be the sheriff,
but I'm a deputy sheriff.

252
00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:04.119
[starts engine]

253
00:20:19.259 --> 00:20:21.429
[groaning]

254
00:20:23.263 --> 00:20:24.597
[groans]

255
00:20:26.433 --> 00:20:28.744
[woman on TV] <i>Little detail</i>
<i>is known of this latest killing,</i>

256
00:20:28.769 --> 00:20:31.480
<i>but the police have identified
the two remaining suspects</i>

257
00:20:31.564 --> 00:20:33.606
<i>in the First Mackey Bank robbery.</i>

258
00:20:33.691 --> 00:20:36.067
<i>Ed Burton and Andrew Sikes.</i>

259
00:20:36.152 --> 00:20:40.197
<i>The owner of the bank, Judge Dawkins,
could not be reached for comment.</i>

260
00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:43.576
<i>But it's now clear that Tuesday's
dramatic shoot-out at the FMB</i>

261
00:20:43.659 --> 00:20:45.661
<i>is anything but over.</i>

262
00:20:45.744 --> 00:20:47.596
<i>- As for the victim, Chris Morrow...</i>
- [phone ringing]

263
00:20:47.621 --> 00:20:49.749
- [mutes TV]
- [phone beeps]

264
00:20:49.832 --> 00:20:53.461
Hey! Listen, you've got to come
and get this money out of here

265
00:20:53.544 --> 00:20:54.878
and give me that tape.

266
00:20:54.961 --> 00:20:57.757
Then just get lost to wherever
the hell you guys are getting lost to.

267
00:20:57.839 --> 00:20:59.633
Don't tell me where.
I don't want to know.

268
00:21:01.384 --> 00:21:05.972
What? But, Ed... Hey, come on!

269
00:21:06.056 --> 00:21:09.351
First, you send me to that motel.
Then, you stick me with this damn bag?

270
00:21:09.434 --> 00:21:14.355
Whoa! No, no, no! We had a deal!
You... Hello? Hello?

271
00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:15.519
[Zeke]
<i>So, what's the story?</i>

272
00:21:15.523 --> 00:21:18.903
Looks like our bank bandits had a dispute
over how to split the proceeds.

273
00:21:18.986 --> 00:21:21.446
Or never planned to split 'em
with this Morrow guy.

274
00:21:21.529 --> 00:21:23.281
[Reed]
Oh, Chris.

275
00:21:25.034 --> 00:21:26.493
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

276
00:21:29.704 --> 00:21:31.957
Your partner doesn't seem
too comfortable around bodies.

277
00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:35.126
Yeah, well, he knew the guy.

278
00:21:35.211 --> 00:21:36.796
You seem all right.

279
00:21:36.878 --> 00:21:39.298
- Yeah, well, I knew the guy.
- Meaning?

280
00:21:39.381 --> 00:21:43.344
Meaning... I'm not too surprised.
Chris was a little slow.

281
00:21:43.426 --> 00:21:46.137
Got his brain fried in a meth lab accident
a few years back.

282
00:21:46.221 --> 00:21:48.807
Same blow-up
that landed Ed Burton in the pen?

283
00:21:48.891 --> 00:21:50.183
That's the one.

284
00:21:50.267 --> 00:21:52.228
Well, that connects them.
What about, uh...?

285
00:21:52.310 --> 00:21:53.770
- My brother?
- Yeah.

286
00:21:53.854 --> 00:21:56.272
You said he knew these other two well.

287
00:21:56.356 --> 00:21:58.292
Well, like I said,
everybody knows everybody well.

288
00:21:58.317 --> 00:22:00.528
Some of us even dated the same girls.

289
00:22:00.611 --> 00:22:02.779
But... there's something else.

290
00:22:04.531 --> 00:22:06.991
Andy was the prosecutor
in the case against Ed and Chris.

291
00:22:07.076 --> 00:22:10.162
Wait. Your brother
is the fucking prosecutor?

292
00:22:10.246 --> 00:22:11.704
He was.

293
00:22:11.788 --> 00:22:13.707
There was a pretty good scandal
after the trial

294
00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:15.711
on account of them
getting such a light sentence.

295
00:22:16.125 --> 00:22:17.126
Nobody proved anything,

296
00:22:17.211 --> 00:22:19.380
but there was a rumor going around
that Ed paid Andy

297
00:22:19.462 --> 00:22:21.423
to drop the reckless manslaughter charges.

298
00:22:21.507 --> 00:22:22.924
Wait, who got manslaughtered?

299
00:22:23.008 --> 00:22:25.051
The file said he got rung up
on meth charges.

300
00:22:26.095 --> 00:22:28.806
When the lab exploded,
Ed's son died in the blast.

301
00:22:28.888 --> 00:22:30.391
Jesus.

302
00:22:31.892 --> 00:22:36.063
Anyway, uh, when the election came around,

303
00:22:36.145 --> 00:22:38.398
my brother got less
than ten percent of the vote.

304
00:22:38.481 --> 00:22:42.278
- You think he took the money?
- No, I, um...

305
00:22:42.361 --> 00:22:44.822
Are you all right there?

306
00:22:44.904 --> 00:22:46.240
Yeah, I, uh...

307
00:22:46.323 --> 00:22:48.491
[takes deep breath]

308
00:22:48.576 --> 00:22:53.079
Stephanie Burton called,
said that Ed came and went.

309
00:23:01.087 --> 00:23:03.464
So he just came back here
to get his clothes?

310
00:23:03.548 --> 00:23:07.469
- He wanted me to go with him.
- And you said no?

311
00:23:08.679 --> 00:23:11.515
- I said no.
- You expect us to believe that?

312
00:23:11.598 --> 00:23:14.852
Ed shows up here with $3 million in cash,
and you just tell him to get lost?

313
00:23:14.934 --> 00:23:19.355
Have you seen my face?
<i>I </i>called <i>you, </i>remember?

314
00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:22.317
Listen, we got a dead body in a county
that doesn't get dead bodies

315
00:23:22.401 --> 00:23:24.153
and a cop with a bullet hole in his arm.

316
00:23:24.236 --> 00:23:25.528
This is a big deal.

317
00:23:25.613 --> 00:23:28.990
So if it turns out that you're lying,
you will end up doin' time.

318
00:23:30.576 --> 00:23:31.576
How much time?

319
00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:33.662
Long enough for you to come out
a different person.

320
00:23:34.496 --> 00:23:36.182
Maybe you lose some
of those girlish good looks.

321
00:23:36.205 --> 00:23:38.041
Maybe you come out an old lady.

322
00:23:38.125 --> 00:23:40.365
- Hey, maybe you don't come out at all.
- [clears throat]

323
00:23:42.046 --> 00:23:43.422
Steph, listen.

324
00:23:43.505 --> 00:23:47.509
- No, you listen. He'll kill me.
- Nobody is killing anybody.

325
00:23:47.593 --> 00:23:49.470
Tell that to Chris Morrow.

326
00:23:49.552 --> 00:23:51.262
Let me rephrase that.

327
00:23:51.346 --> 00:23:55.601
The best way for nobody else to get killed
is for you to tell us what you know.

328
00:24:03.192 --> 00:24:04.192
He's going to Mexico.

329
00:24:05.402 --> 00:24:07.202
He said he had one more thing
to take care of,

330
00:24:07.278 --> 00:24:09.448
but don't ask me what
because I don't know.

331
00:24:11.532 --> 00:24:13.826
Ed isn't much into discussing
business with me.

332
00:24:17.955 --> 00:24:19.583
- So what do you think?
- I don't know.

333
00:24:19.666 --> 00:24:21.501
What do you think
that one more thing was?

334
00:24:21.585 --> 00:24:22.670
Could be Andy.

335
00:24:22.752 --> 00:24:26.423
- You don't think they're together?
- No, I never thought they were together.

336
00:24:26.507 --> 00:24:27.508
I think Ed was planning

337
00:24:27.590 --> 00:24:29.527
- to rip those guys off from moment one.
- [phone ringing]

338
00:24:29.550 --> 00:24:31.345
So what do we do now?

339
00:24:31.428 --> 00:24:33.137
Sikes. Hang on a sec.

340
00:24:36.683 --> 00:24:39.435
- Where are you?
- Mexico. You should check it out.

341
00:24:39.519 --> 00:24:42.021
Drinks are a bit pricey,
but the beaches are amazing.

342
00:24:42.105 --> 00:24:43.147
<i>Gosh, I'd really love to,</i>

343
00:24:43.231 --> 00:24:46.693
but I'm kinda busy right now
hunting down my brother.

344
00:24:46.777 --> 00:24:48.987
Don't bother. I told you, I'm in Mexico.

345
00:24:49.904 --> 00:24:52.740
<i>Jesus, Andy.
What the hell were you thinking?</i>

346
00:24:52.825 --> 00:24:56.452
What was I thinking?
Look at me. My life is in ruins.

347
00:24:56.537 --> 00:24:59.998
I'm doing nothing but quickie divorces
and hawking life insurance.

348
00:25:00.082 --> 00:25:02.769
Yeah, maybe you should've thought of that
before you took Ed's money.

349
00:25:02.792 --> 00:25:05.753
I told you, man, I didn't take Ed's money.

350
00:25:05.837 --> 00:25:09.633
<i>Really? After all that's happened,
you're still gonna lie to me?</i>

351
00:25:11.300 --> 00:25:12.635
I don't know what to say.

352
00:25:12.720 --> 00:25:16.557
<i>I want to you admit that Ed paid you
to drop the reckless manslaughter charge.</i>

353
00:25:16.640 --> 00:25:20.810
I want you to admit you traded
a little boy's life for a fancy car.

354
00:25:20.894 --> 00:25:24.940
You make it sound so simple.
What about Judge Dawkins?

355
00:25:25.022 --> 00:25:26.983
Nobody cares
that he signed off on Ed's plea deal.

356
00:25:27.067 --> 00:25:29.862
We're not talking about Judge Dawkins.
We're talking about my brother.

357
00:25:29.944 --> 00:25:31.238
We're talking about you.

358
00:25:33.281 --> 00:25:34.407
Okay.

359
00:25:36.492 --> 00:25:37.618
Fine.

360
00:25:39.829 --> 00:25:41.539
Ed bought me off.

361
00:25:42.415 --> 00:25:45.794
Okay? You happy?

362
00:25:46.753 --> 00:25:49.506
Andy, you need to turn yourself in.

363
00:25:49.589 --> 00:25:50.589
[scoffs]

364
00:25:50.590 --> 00:25:53.301
Turn myself in? Are you kidding me?
With Chris dead?

365
00:25:53.384 --> 00:25:55.304
<i>Now that's fucking felony-murder.</i>

366
00:25:55.386 --> 00:25:58.640
Andy, I can't get you out of this.

367
00:25:59.892 --> 00:26:04.104
You either turn yourself in
or you face the consequences.

368
00:26:19.076 --> 00:26:21.413
- Where'd the Feds go?
- They went to check on a lead.

369
00:26:21.497 --> 00:26:23.707
The old barn. The Metcamp property.

370
00:26:23.790 --> 00:26:27.126
- Someone found Chris's Caddy.
- Really?

371
00:26:27.211 --> 00:26:29.505
I think we should have the Feds
camp out here tonight,

372
00:26:29.587 --> 00:26:30.838
keep an eye on Steph,

373
00:26:30.923 --> 00:26:33.299
in case Ed gets any bright ideas.

374
00:26:33.383 --> 00:26:36.135
- You know, two guys he doesn't recognize.
- That makes sense.

375
00:26:37.346 --> 00:26:40.723
- Hey, who was that? Martha?
- Yeah, sloppy joes tonight.

376
00:26:42.017 --> 00:26:44.603
I love a sloppy joe.

377
00:26:44.685 --> 00:26:50.025
Except, this morning, you told me
you were having fried chicken, Zeke.

378
00:26:50.107 --> 00:26:51.652
Who was that? Your brother?

379
00:26:54.863 --> 00:26:55.905
You really want to know?

380
00:26:57.074 --> 00:27:00.117
I just don't want you to get yourself
into something you can't get out of.

381
00:27:00.993 --> 00:27:02.763
[scoffs] Reed, how long
have we known each other?

382
00:27:02.788 --> 00:27:05.540
- That's not the point. Blood is blood.
- Exactly.

383
00:27:05.624 --> 00:27:08.919
So let's just leave it at that. Okay?

384
00:27:09.001 --> 00:27:10.671
All right, let's do it.

385
00:27:12.297 --> 00:27:13.464
So, what is it?

386
00:27:14.799 --> 00:27:17.553
- You having sloppy joes or fried chicken?
- Who cares?

387
00:27:24.351 --> 00:27:27.813
[man] It's me. No, baby, listen.
Don't hang up. Don't hang up.

388
00:27:27.895 --> 00:27:31.232
I know I said
that I'd never call you again

389
00:27:31.316 --> 00:27:34.694
but I just could use
a little company right now.

390
00:27:34.778 --> 00:27:37.197
Stop, no, no. Stop. Don't hang up.

391
00:27:38.740 --> 00:27:40.616
I'll pay.

392
00:27:41.576 --> 00:27:44.121
I know you're not a whore.

393
00:27:44.203 --> 00:27:45.998
No, I'm not implying anything.

394
00:27:46.080 --> 00:27:47.583
I just... I just...

395
00:27:49.375 --> 00:27:50.669
I'm desperate.

396
00:27:51.878 --> 00:27:54.673
A thousand dollars?
What, are you insane?

397
00:27:54.756 --> 00:27:57.718
Stop, stop! I know.
No, you're fine. You're right.

398
00:27:57.800 --> 00:28:00.971
A thousand dollars is right.
Just get over here.

399
00:28:26.288 --> 00:28:27.288
[laughing]

400
00:28:27.372 --> 00:28:29.625
It's very, very good. It's very good.

401
00:28:29.708 --> 00:28:32.794
Well, thank you, Ezekiel.
That's awful kind of you to say.

402
00:28:32.877 --> 00:28:34.546
Isn't that nice of him to say, Sally?

403
00:28:35.463 --> 00:28:36.589
[giggling]

404
00:28:37.214 --> 00:28:39.800
What is so funny, little miss giggles?

405
00:28:39.884 --> 00:28:42.221
I swear, sometimes, I don't know
what to do with this one.

406
00:28:42.304 --> 00:28:44.472
Are you gonna be my new daddy?

407
00:28:44.556 --> 00:28:46.098
[Martha coughs]

408
00:28:49.936 --> 00:28:52.730
Sally, now listen here.

409
00:28:53.856 --> 00:28:58.487
Your daddy is gonna be home very soon
safe and sound, okay?

410
00:28:59.278 --> 00:29:04.326
Now, eat that chicken so you can grow up
big and strong like your daddy

411
00:29:04.409 --> 00:29:07.371
and not small and weak like me.

412
00:29:07.453 --> 00:29:08.579
Okay.

413
00:29:09.623 --> 00:29:12.416
I tell you, you sure have a way
with the little ones.

414
00:29:12.500 --> 00:29:15.086
Why didn't you ever settle down
and have one of your own?

415
00:29:15.170 --> 00:29:17.609
Sally Ann Sikes, what in God's name
do you think you're doing?

416
00:29:17.631 --> 00:29:19.215
[Sally giggling]

417
00:29:19.298 --> 00:29:23.053
[chuckles] On second thought,
consider yourself lucky.

418
00:29:23.135 --> 00:29:26.597
- Give me that.
- [Sally giggling]

419
00:29:29.476 --> 00:29:31.144
You are so beautiful.

420
00:29:35.523 --> 00:29:36.732
[lighter clicking]

421
00:29:45.450 --> 00:29:46.785
I tell you, this is way better

422
00:29:46.867 --> 00:29:49.829
than anything that degenerate Ed
used to cook up.

423
00:29:51.205 --> 00:29:52.708
Ed is such a two-bit hustler.

424
00:29:52.790 --> 00:29:56.961
He used to cook his shit
with, like, MSM, Lexapro.

425
00:29:57.045 --> 00:29:59.172
You name it, he used it.

426
00:29:59.256 --> 00:30:00.298
But this stuff...

427
00:30:00.382 --> 00:30:04.635
I mean, for a thousand bucks,
I went straight to the magic man.

428
00:30:05.386 --> 00:30:06.805
Can I have a kiss?

429
00:30:14.813 --> 00:30:18.482
- I thought you were still mad at me.
- [scoffs]

430
00:30:18.567 --> 00:30:20.777
No, I was never mad at you.

431
00:30:20.861 --> 00:30:26.615
You were young, you needed money.
It's an opportunity. You took it.

432
00:30:26.700 --> 00:30:29.786
I was mostly mad at myself
for being so weak.

433
00:30:38.795 --> 00:30:40.797
- [stomach grumbling]
- Oh...

434
00:30:40.881 --> 00:30:43.967
- You okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

435
00:30:45.594 --> 00:30:47.346
I just gotta take a shit, that's all.

436
00:30:48.721 --> 00:30:51.182
- How romantic.
- Oh, sorry, honey.

437
00:30:51.266 --> 00:30:53.268
It's not you. It's the drugs.

438
00:30:53.352 --> 00:30:56.104
Sometimes, these things
just flush me right out.

439
00:30:59.648 --> 00:31:01.067
[sighs]

440
00:31:03.319 --> 00:31:06.615
- Andy! What the hell are you doing here?
- I want the money.

441
00:31:06.698 --> 00:31:10.117
- [stutters] Why would I have the money?
- Don't you play fucking dumb with me!

442
00:31:10.201 --> 00:31:11.281
- I don't have it!
- Really?

443
00:31:11.327 --> 00:31:14.914
- You haven't seen Ed recently?
- I'm afraid you've been misinformed.

444
00:31:14.998 --> 00:31:17.375
You should be afraid
that I'm gonna shoot you in the...

445
00:31:20.878 --> 00:31:22.672
Seriously? Under the fuckin' bed?

446
00:31:22.756 --> 00:31:25.037
You didn't think I was gonna search
under the goddamn bed?

447
00:31:25.049 --> 00:31:26.861
- [groaning]
- Andy, think about what you're doing.

448
00:31:26.884 --> 00:31:29.261
- Ed will kill you...
- Fuck Ed!

449
00:31:29.346 --> 00:31:31.847
He should be afraid I'm gonna kill him!

450
00:31:33.557 --> 00:31:36.603
- [groaning]
- [stomach grumbling]

451
00:31:40.315 --> 00:31:43.692
You know, I just don't get it.
Why are you helping him?

452
00:31:44.653 --> 00:31:45.862
None of your business.

453
00:31:47.447 --> 00:31:53.119
Look, you have your money, right?
Why don't you just go?

454
00:31:53.202 --> 00:31:56.789
You've got everything.
You've got a career.

455
00:31:56.873 --> 00:31:59.417
In fact, I heard you're running
for the goddamn Senate.

456
00:32:01.377 --> 00:32:02.711
What does Ed have on you?

457
00:32:02.796 --> 00:32:07.884
Enough. He's got enough.
Please, just go.

458
00:32:07.968 --> 00:32:10.095
No, no, no.

459
00:32:10.178 --> 00:32:13.181
- See you around, Judge.
- [sighs]

460
00:32:13.265 --> 00:32:16.643
[defecating loudly]
Oh!

461
00:32:16.726 --> 00:32:19.520
What the fuck? Someone's in there.

462
00:32:21.230 --> 00:32:23.817
- Is it Ed? I'm gonna fucking kill him.
- No, it's not Ed.

463
00:32:23.900 --> 00:32:25.943
Please don't open that door,
I'm begging you.

464
00:32:26.027 --> 00:32:27.867
- Get your hands off me!
- Andy, I'm on my knees.

465
00:32:27.903 --> 00:32:29.364
Please, let's just talk about it.

466
00:32:29.448 --> 00:32:31.782
Once you open that door,
there's no going back.

467
00:32:33.910 --> 00:32:34.910
[grunts]

468
00:32:36.371 --> 00:32:38.832
[screaming]

469
00:32:38.914 --> 00:32:40.333
What the fuck? Oh!

470
00:32:41.750 --> 00:32:46.173
- [both grunting]
- [screaming]

471
00:32:47.715 --> 00:32:49.718
[screaming]

472
00:32:51.760 --> 00:32:55.307
- [screaming]
- [both grunting]

473
00:33:12.240 --> 00:33:14.159
Allison, do you know
where my slippers are?

474
00:33:17.244 --> 00:33:18.497
Allison?

475
00:33:20.039 --> 00:33:22.041
Hey, Allison, do you know
where my slippers are?

476
00:33:22.125 --> 00:33:23.335
I can't find 'em.

477
00:33:30.884 --> 00:33:33.385
I need my slippers, Ally.

478
00:33:44.021 --> 00:33:45.440
[flushes toilet]

479
00:33:49.443 --> 00:33:50.444
Get the hell out here!

480
00:33:52.530 --> 00:33:55.075
Stop! Get on your knees.

481
00:33:57.576 --> 00:33:59.746
Please, I won't say anything, I swear!

482
00:33:59.828 --> 00:34:02.332
- That's what everybody says.
- Jesus, you've done this before?

483
00:34:02.414 --> 00:34:04.084
No. No, I...

484
00:34:05.751 --> 00:34:06.920
I just don't believe you.

485
00:34:07.002 --> 00:34:09.755
- I'm just a kid. Who am I gonna tell?
- Shut up.

486
00:34:11.007 --> 00:34:12.007
Turn around.

487
00:34:18.974 --> 00:34:21.476
- What's happening?
- Shut up! Stop talking!

488
00:34:22.978 --> 00:34:24.353
Our Father, Who art in heaven...

489
00:34:25.105 --> 00:34:26.981
Stop praying!

490
00:34:28.148 --> 00:34:30.068
God!

491
00:34:31.652 --> 00:34:34.239
If you tell one goddamn soul,
I will fucking kill you.

492
00:34:34.322 --> 00:34:36.365
I was never here.

493
00:34:36.907 --> 00:34:38.242
Get out!

494
00:34:58.346 --> 00:35:01.682
[Walker]
Good night, Steph. Sleep tight.

495
00:35:03.934 --> 00:35:06.563
[Biltmore] Let me ask you something.
Do you think my wife's hot?

496
00:35:06.646 --> 00:35:09.356
Yeah. Hot enough.

497
00:35:09.440 --> 00:35:12.027
What do you mean "hot enough"?
<i>My</i> wife?

498
00:35:12.110 --> 00:35:16.072
Yeah, she's... I mean... I said she's hot.
She's hot enough. She's hot. She's...

499
00:35:16.155 --> 00:35:17.476
What do you mean by "hot enough"?

500
00:35:17.489 --> 00:35:19.490
- She's plenty hot.
- You qualified it with "enough."

501
00:35:19.534 --> 00:35:21.637
- She's plenty hot enough?
- I said she was fuckin' hot!

502
00:35:21.661 --> 00:35:23.038
Fuck you.

503
00:35:23.121 --> 00:35:25.873
Fuckin' hotter than Margaret.

504
00:35:25.956 --> 00:35:28.751
Oh, shit. They forgot my chalupa.

505
00:35:32.880 --> 00:35:34.423
- What the fuck is that?
- What?

506
00:35:34.507 --> 00:35:35.925
The naked kid!

507
00:35:36.009 --> 00:35:38.260
What naked kid?
I was looking for my chalupa.

508
00:35:38.344 --> 00:35:42.974
Fuck the fucking chalupa!
A bummed-out crackhead just streaked us.

509
00:35:43.057 --> 00:35:45.934
[chuckles]

510
00:35:46.018 --> 00:35:47.936
Okey-doke.

511
00:35:48.021 --> 00:35:52.067
I think it's time for someone
to cut out the hot sauce.

512
00:36:52.168 --> 00:36:53.795
<i>Andy?</i>

513
00:36:53.878 --> 00:36:55.755
Andy, are you awake?

514
00:37:00.885 --> 00:37:01.927
[whistling]

515
00:37:06.516 --> 00:37:07.516
Bah!

516
00:37:14.815 --> 00:37:19.487
- Hey, what happened last night?
- Shh! Just give me a minute.

517
00:37:21.447 --> 00:37:23.074
[groans]

518
00:37:23.157 --> 00:37:25.702
[sniffles, sighs]

519
00:37:27.536 --> 00:37:29.748
- What?
- What happened last night?

520
00:37:30.831 --> 00:37:32.601
What do you mean,
what fucking happened last night?

521
00:37:32.625 --> 00:37:37.088
- Ed fucked us is what happened.
- No, he wouldn't do that.

522
00:37:38.547 --> 00:37:42.385
Listen, Chris, I know that something's
wrong with you up in the head,

523
00:37:42.469 --> 00:37:46.264
but please don't say that Ed wouldn't
do that when he just fucking did that!

524
00:37:47.556 --> 00:37:51.059
- No way.
- Jesus Christ, you're stupid.

525
00:37:51.143 --> 00:37:54.146
- Don't call me stupid, Andy.
- Don't be stupid, then.

526
00:37:54.230 --> 00:37:55.481
[sighs]

527
00:38:00.068 --> 00:38:04.364
- What should we do?
- Check the radio.

528
00:38:05.867 --> 00:38:06.909
[turns on radio]

529
00:38:06.992 --> 00:38:09.077
[static]

530
00:38:09.161 --> 00:38:11.206
[instrumental music playing]

531
00:38:20.047 --> 00:38:23.635
Are you fucking kidding me?
You dipshit! The news!

532
00:38:25.385 --> 00:38:27.096
[static]

533
00:38:27.179 --> 00:38:30.474
[man] <i>...have been identified</i>
<i>as Edward Burton, Andrew Sikes,</i>

534
00:38:30.557 --> 00:38:31.434
<i>and Chris Morrow.</i>

535
00:38:31.518 --> 00:38:34.269
<i>All three suspects are considered
armed and dangerous.</i>

536
00:38:34.353 --> 00:38:38.315
<i>Sheriff Ezekiel Sikes was shot and wounded
as he attempted to foil the robbery.</i>

537
00:38:38.398 --> 00:38:43.445
Ed shot Zeke? Holy shit!
Hey, where are you going?

538
00:38:44.405 --> 00:38:47.199
- I've gotta call my brother.
- Are you nuts?

539
00:38:47.282 --> 00:38:49.994
- He's the one who ratted us out.
- We don't know that for sure.

540
00:38:50.077 --> 00:38:51.621
Who else could it be?

541
00:38:51.704 --> 00:38:56.166
Oh, gee, Chris, maybe it was the cops
who pulled us over for speeding

542
00:38:56.251 --> 00:38:58.961
half a mile from the fucking bank!

543
00:38:59.045 --> 00:39:01.588
- We were making a getaway.
- Ugh!

544
00:39:01.672 --> 00:39:03.675
I'll take you. I'll just drive you.

545
00:39:03.757 --> 00:39:07.052
No, no! Listen, cockbrain,
you've gotta get your shit together.

546
00:39:07.135 --> 00:39:08.262
Your car is blazing hot.

547
00:39:08.346 --> 00:39:10.181
- You gotta stash it somewhere.
- Where?

548
00:39:10.264 --> 00:39:12.432
Anywhere. One of the barns
around here or something.

549
00:39:12.516 --> 00:39:13.601
Okay, then what?

550
00:39:15.103 --> 00:39:16.144
Okay.

551
00:39:17.021 --> 00:39:20.190
Chris, listen to me. Listen good, okay?

552
00:39:20.275 --> 00:39:22.818
You are gonna stash your car
in one of these barns.

553
00:39:22.902 --> 00:39:25.195
Then, you are gonna do nothing.
You are gonna say there.

554
00:39:25.280 --> 00:39:27.197
You're gonna stay put.
Do you understand me?

555
00:39:27.282 --> 00:39:32.619
Until tonight. You are gonna meet me
at ten o'clock at Rudy's scrapyard.

556
00:39:32.704 --> 00:39:35.123
Okay? By then, I should know
more of what's going on.

557
00:39:35.206 --> 00:39:36.373
Rudy's scrapyard, ten.

558
00:39:36.456 --> 00:39:38.418
- You have a watch?
- Sure, yeah.

559
00:39:38.501 --> 00:39:40.878
- Know how to tell time?
- It's digital.

560
00:39:40.961 --> 00:39:44.923
Okay, and if you get caught,
you don't know anything.

561
00:39:46.217 --> 00:39:47.302
Shouldn't be a problem.

562
00:39:50.637 --> 00:39:55.518
- You're not all gone, are you, Chris?
- Not yet, no.

563
00:40:16.706 --> 00:40:17.706
[groans]

564
00:40:34.932 --> 00:40:38.143
[vehicle approaching]

565
00:40:39.811 --> 00:40:43.148
Sorry I'm late.
I saw her coming back from the cemetery.

566
00:40:43.231 --> 00:40:45.585
Figured it was better
than sitting in front of an empty house.

567
00:40:45.610 --> 00:40:46.610
Uh-huh.

568
00:40:51.114 --> 00:40:54.619
- [sighs] Hey, Steph, how you feeling?
- How am I feeling?

569
00:40:54.702 --> 00:40:58.414
Like the idiot wife of an ex-con
who just shot a cop and split town.

570
00:40:58.498 --> 00:41:01.833
- How are you feeling?
- Not great, either.

571
00:41:03.293 --> 00:41:04.293
[sighs]

572
00:41:08.840 --> 00:41:12.719
Has Ed been acting strange at all, lately?
You notice anything?

573
00:41:12.804 --> 00:41:16.349
Strange how? Like, did I see him
with a bunch of his scumbag friends

574
00:41:16.431 --> 00:41:17.576
sitting around the kitchen table,

575
00:41:17.599 --> 00:41:19.518
going over the blueprints
of the local bank,

576
00:41:19.601 --> 00:41:21.938
talking about how they were gonna rob it?

577
00:41:22.021 --> 00:41:23.898
Yeah, uh, yeah, like that.

578
00:41:25.440 --> 00:41:26.943
Be back in a sec.

579
00:41:28.152 --> 00:41:31.239
You know, I'm just asking questions.
You don't have to be mean.

580
00:41:32.489 --> 00:41:35.451
- I take it you're Sheriff Sikes?
- Zeke.

581
00:41:35.534 --> 00:41:38.579
- How's your shoulder, Zeke?
- Eh, it hurts.

582
00:41:38.663 --> 00:41:40.331
Yeah, I'm sure it does.

583
00:41:40.414 --> 00:41:42.333
- Kurt Biltmore. This here's Kyle Walker.
- Hey.

584
00:41:42.416 --> 00:41:46.211
Kurt, Kyle. Mind if I speak first?

585
00:41:47.005 --> 00:41:48.715
By all means.

586
00:41:48.797 --> 00:41:50.717
Fellas, this here is a local matter.

587
00:41:50.800 --> 00:41:54.012
It's a local crime committed
by locals against locals.

588
00:41:54.094 --> 00:41:56.054
Shit, as I'm sure you're aware,

589
00:41:56.139 --> 00:41:59.224
one of the guys involved
is my own goddamn brother.

590
00:41:59.307 --> 00:42:01.507
In high school, we all played
on the same football team.

591
00:42:01.518 --> 00:42:03.228
We all know each other, so...

592
00:42:03.311 --> 00:42:06.983
I assure you, if anybody's capable
of catching these guys,

593
00:42:07.065 --> 00:42:08.960
catching them
before there's any further bloodshed,

594
00:42:08.985 --> 00:42:11.112
it's gonna be my partner and I.

595
00:42:11.195 --> 00:42:13.697
That being said,
when it comes time to make arrests,

596
00:42:13.780 --> 00:42:16.492
you guys feel free
to take every ounce of credit.

597
00:42:16.576 --> 00:42:19.829
So, if you don't mind
taking a bit of a back seat,

598
00:42:19.911 --> 00:42:21.748
we'll be happy to paint you
as the heroes.

599
00:42:21.831 --> 00:42:23.248
How's that sound?

600
00:42:23.331 --> 00:42:24.751
- May I?
- Oh, by all means.

601
00:42:24.833 --> 00:42:25.833
Okay.

602
00:42:26.585 --> 00:42:28.463
Zeke, I appreciate
your being frank with us,

603
00:42:28.545 --> 00:42:30.380
so I'm gonna go ahead
and return the favor.

604
00:42:30.465 --> 00:42:31.882
And go ahead and stop me

605
00:42:31.965 --> 00:42:34.844
if I say something
that rubs you the wrong way, okay?

606
00:42:34.927 --> 00:42:37.096
We understand
that what happened here last night

607
00:42:37.179 --> 00:42:39.931
is a very serious matter
around these parts,

608
00:42:40.016 --> 00:42:44.936
but, as far as the Bureau's concerned,
it's not exactly 9/11 part two.

609
00:42:45.021 --> 00:42:48.148
You know? If it wasn't for the fact
that the bank is federally insured,

610
00:42:48.231 --> 00:42:51.402
then we would not be down here
messing around in your affairs.

611
00:42:51.485 --> 00:42:55.197
So, if you were expecting
a couple of, uh... [chuckles]

612
00:42:55.280 --> 00:42:59.034
Grizzled FBI guys charging in here
and giving you the high hat,

613
00:42:59.117 --> 00:43:02.454
well, you're gonna be happily mistaken.

614
00:43:02.538 --> 00:43:04.289
Kurt and I are like the B team.

615
00:43:04.373 --> 00:43:06.751
Well, we're like the B team to the D team.

616
00:43:06.833 --> 00:43:08.251
Yeah, we're the E team.

617
00:43:08.335 --> 00:43:10.880
So your arrangement sounds
just perfect to us.

618
00:43:10.963 --> 00:43:14.467
All right. Sounds like we're gonna
get along just fine.

619
00:43:14.550 --> 00:43:17.052
Reed Ethington,
I'd like you to meet the two gentlemen

620
00:43:17.135 --> 00:43:20.389
our government has sent down here
to assist us in our hour of need.

621
00:43:20.472 --> 00:43:22.557
So, let's head over to Morrow's place.

622
00:43:22.641 --> 00:43:26.103
If any of 'em are dumb enough
to head home, it'd have to be Chris.

623
00:43:26.186 --> 00:43:27.355
We'll follow you.

624
00:43:55.298 --> 00:43:56.884
[whistling]

625
00:43:56.967 --> 00:44:00.637
What's a nice girl like you
doing in a place like this?

626
00:44:00.721 --> 00:44:02.306
It's my brother's car.

627
00:44:02.389 --> 00:44:05.309
Your brother, the bank robber,
drives a Porsche?

628
00:44:05.393 --> 00:44:08.436
It's an example of how the local knowledge
might come in handy.

629
00:44:08.521 --> 00:44:11.273
- I'll say.
- Care to elaborate?

630
00:44:12.775 --> 00:44:15.610
It's complicated. Let's just see
what we find in Morrow's place.

631
00:44:18.655 --> 00:44:21.032
Mice, I'm guessing.

632
00:44:21.117 --> 00:44:24.036
Or a raccoon. Maybe a sheep.

633
00:44:24.119 --> 00:44:25.954
Chris?

634
00:44:27.581 --> 00:44:29.500
Chris, it's Zeke Sikes!

635
00:44:32.128 --> 00:44:33.378
Chris?

636
00:44:45.599 --> 00:44:46.766
Chris?

637
00:44:55.067 --> 00:44:56.818
Chris, Zeke Sikes!

638
00:44:58.153 --> 00:44:59.572
If you're in there...

639
00:45:08.998 --> 00:45:10.498
I'm coming in!

640
00:45:15.795 --> 00:45:18.673
Ma'am, I'm gonna need you to get up!

641
00:45:26.389 --> 00:45:27.557
Chris...

642
00:45:30.393 --> 00:45:31.646
[sheep bleating]

643
00:45:32.980 --> 00:45:34.019
[phone ringing, vibrating]

644
00:45:36.817 --> 00:45:38.737
- [chicken clucking]
- [phone ringing, vibrating]

645
00:45:38.818 --> 00:45:40.445
[sheep bleating]

646
00:45:41.112 --> 00:45:42.364
[phone ringing, vibrating]

647
00:45:47.536 --> 00:45:48.746
[sheep bleating]

648
00:45:50.206 --> 00:45:51.456
[cow mooing]

649
00:45:52.248 --> 00:45:53.458
[chicken clucking]

650
00:45:53.541 --> 00:45:56.003
- Hello?
<i>- Hey, Chris, it's Steph.</i>

651
00:45:57.588 --> 00:45:59.923
- Steph, really?
<i>- Where are you?</i>

652
00:46:00.007 --> 00:46:03.635
- [cow mooing]
- Oh! Uh, no, I-I can't say.

653
00:46:03.719 --> 00:46:07.722
- Listen, Ed called. He wants to meet up.
<i>- He does?</i>

654
00:46:07.806 --> 00:46:10.476
<i>- Andy said he tried to screw us over.</i>
- That's not true.

655
00:46:10.559 --> 00:46:12.769
Zeke took a shot at him.
Ed had to shoot back.

656
00:46:12.853 --> 00:46:14.896
He made a break for it,
same as you guys.

657
00:46:14.981 --> 00:46:16.983
No, no, not the same as us

658
00:46:17.065 --> 00:46:19.402
because he's the one
that ended up with all the money.

659
00:46:19.485 --> 00:46:22.195
Right, well, he wants to settle up,
split the cash,

660
00:46:22.278 --> 00:46:24.114
and then we all go our separate ways.

661
00:46:24.197 --> 00:46:25.197
<i>Well...</i>

662
00:46:28.327 --> 00:46:31.414
I can't go nowhere
until after I meet up with Andy at ten.

663
00:46:31.496 --> 00:46:33.206
<i>No, Chris, just you.</i>

664
00:46:33.289 --> 00:46:36.168
<i>Ed doesn't trust
that Andy won't do something stupid.</i>

665
00:46:36.251 --> 00:46:38.086
<i>But he can trust you, right?</i>

666
00:46:39.295 --> 00:46:41.507
Of course, he can trust me.

667
00:46:41.590 --> 00:46:43.300
Good. You have a pen?

668
00:46:43.384 --> 00:46:46.721
- Where's Daddy?
- Oh, Daddy had to work late, sugarplum.

669
00:46:47.804 --> 00:46:50.056
I mean, you know,
this is all just a big mistake.

670
00:46:50.141 --> 00:46:53.101
Andy would never get involved
in anything like this.

671
00:46:54.186 --> 00:46:58.190
Martha, I saw him there
with my own two eyes.

672
00:46:58.273 --> 00:47:01.068
Well, your eyes deceived you,
plain and simple.

673
00:47:01.152 --> 00:47:06.532
- Oh, yeah? Then where the hell is Daddy?
- He's working late, goddamn it!

674
00:47:10.202 --> 00:47:13.664
I'm sorry. I know you're upset, too.

675
00:47:15.041 --> 00:47:19.210
- Hey, how's your shoulder?
- What happened to your shoulder?

676
00:47:20.628 --> 00:47:24.884
- I fell and bumped into a tree.
- That was pretty silly.

677
00:47:27.385 --> 00:47:30.722
Yeah, well... I'm a pretty silly guy.

678
00:47:35.811 --> 00:47:36.853
See ya!

679
00:47:38.063 --> 00:47:39.190
[speaking Spanish]

680
00:47:39.273 --> 00:47:41.525
<i>Gracias, amigos.</i>

681
00:47:41.608 --> 00:47:43.860
<i>- Adi? s.</i>
- Peace.

682
00:47:43.943 --> 00:47:44.987
<i>Adi? s.</i>

683
00:47:50.617 --> 00:47:52.786
- Chris!
- Steph?

684
00:47:52.869 --> 00:47:55.581
- Over here.
- Is that you?

685
00:47:55.664 --> 00:47:56.916
Hurry up!

686
00:47:58.833 --> 00:48:01.003
Hey, I made it!

687
00:48:06.800 --> 00:48:09.969
Is that... Is that what I think it is?

688
00:48:11.347 --> 00:48:12.847
Shit.

689
00:48:13.389 --> 00:48:17.061
- Chris, have you changed your clothes?
- Since when?

690
00:48:17.143 --> 00:48:21.231
- Since you robbed the bank?
- Oh, no.

691
00:48:21.315 --> 00:48:22.858
Here. Put on something of Ed's.

692
00:48:25.068 --> 00:48:26.820
Where is Ed anyway?

693
00:48:26.903 --> 00:48:29.614
He went to get a passport.
We're going to Mexico.

694
00:48:29.697 --> 00:48:32.867
- [shower running]
- Oh, well, that's smart.

695
00:48:32.952 --> 00:48:34.954
Ed's a smart guy.

696
00:48:35.913 --> 00:48:38.791
Listen, do you mind
if I hop in the shower?

697
00:48:39.708 --> 00:48:41.876
You want to take a shower?

698
00:48:41.960 --> 00:48:43.420
Mm-hmm.

699
00:48:45.130 --> 00:48:46.130
Uh...

700
00:48:46.465 --> 00:48:48.384
Yeah. Okay.

701
00:49:01.480 --> 00:49:06.777
I always figured you sorta hated me
on account of what happened to Ed Jr.

702
00:49:09.405 --> 00:49:10.780
That was an accident.

703
00:49:13.992 --> 00:49:17.036
Put your gun down, Chris. Relax.

704
00:49:47.358 --> 00:49:48.568
Who the hell are you?

705
00:49:49.527 --> 00:49:52.072
You know who I am, son.
I'm Judge Dawkins.

706
00:49:52.155 --> 00:49:54.115
What the hell are you doing here?

707
00:49:54.199 --> 00:49:57.202
Well, Ed and Steph asked me to...

708
00:49:57.286 --> 00:49:59.329
Chris, don't trust him.

709
00:49:59.413 --> 00:50:01.539
Steph, what the hell's going on?

710
00:50:01.623 --> 00:50:04.293
Chris, if he takes the money,
we'll never see a penny of it.

711
00:50:04.376 --> 00:50:07.086
I don't want the money.
Steph, what the hell are you doing?

712
00:50:07.170 --> 00:50:09.882
Chris, he's lying.

713
00:50:09.965 --> 00:50:13.469
Hey, give me my gun back.
Give me back my gun!

714
00:50:13.552 --> 00:50:14.929
All right. Hold on, Chris.

715
00:50:15.012 --> 00:50:16.739
- We're gonna slow this down.
- Chris, don't trust him.

716
00:50:16.764 --> 00:50:18.574
Just give me the tape
and leave me out of this!

717
00:50:18.599 --> 00:50:19.849
No! Give me back my gun back!

718
00:50:19.934 --> 00:50:21.494
- We're gonna slow it down.
- Chris, he's lying.

719
00:50:21.518 --> 00:50:22.518
Don't do anything stupid.

720
00:50:22.603 --> 00:50:25.396
- Did you just call me stupid?
- Don't... Don't come further.

721
00:50:25.481 --> 00:50:26.606
'Cause I ain't stupid, okay?

722
00:50:26.690 --> 00:50:29.001
- All right, hold on.
- You people are always calling me names!

723
00:50:29.025 --> 00:50:30.586
- Don't come any further.
- But you don't know me!

724
00:50:30.610 --> 00:50:33.197
- I was smart once!
- I have a gun in my hand! Stop! I have...

725
00:50:43.831 --> 00:50:45.751
Jesus, Judge.

726
00:50:46.751 --> 00:50:51.047
I didn't... I didn't...
What have I... What have I done?

727
00:50:51.130 --> 00:50:52.632
You killed him.

728
00:50:52.715 --> 00:50:56.679
You provoked him!
Why did you provoke him?

729
00:50:56.762 --> 00:50:57.887
Just making sure.

730
00:50:59.222 --> 00:51:01.641
- You manipulative little sh...
- Focus, Judge.

731
00:51:01.724 --> 00:51:05.144
You just emptied a machine gun.
There's gonna be cops all over this place.

732
00:51:05.228 --> 00:51:08.815
- Ed. Where the fuck is Ed?
- Ed's keeping a low profile.

733
00:51:08.898 --> 00:51:11.277
There's way too much heat on him
to risk being seen.

734
00:51:11.360 --> 00:51:12.485
All right, where's my tape?

735
00:51:12.568 --> 00:51:14.570
We'll give it to you
when we come pick up the bag.

736
00:51:14.655 --> 00:51:16.739
No! I don't want the bag! I want the tape!

737
00:51:16.824 --> 00:51:20.327
We need you to hold on to the money for
a couple days until things cool off a bit.

738
00:51:20.411 --> 00:51:21.829
No, no, no. Just give me the tape.

739
00:51:21.911 --> 00:51:24.266
I'm gonna get out of here. I don't wanna
have anything to do with this.

740
00:51:24.289 --> 00:51:26.309
It's just a day or two,
and then this will all be over.

741
00:51:26.333 --> 00:51:30.378
No! This has gone too far.

742
00:51:30.461 --> 00:51:34.007
Just make sure your wife and kids
aren't around for a few days.

743
00:51:34.090 --> 00:51:37.677
'Cause we want to keep this thing
nice and simple, right?

744
00:51:39.096 --> 00:51:40.764
See you soon, Judge.

745
00:51:53.985 --> 00:51:55.737
"Rudy's scrapyard at ten."

746
00:51:55.820 --> 00:51:58.114
[imitating Chris]
"I got it. Okay. I'll see you there."

747
00:51:58.197 --> 00:52:00.492
Fucking asshole!

748
00:52:00.576 --> 00:52:01.577
[grunts]

749
00:52:01.659 --> 00:52:03.369
[clock ticking]

750
00:52:08.541 --> 00:52:10.001
Shh.

751
00:52:17.384 --> 00:52:20.512
- What the heck are you doing?
- Huh? Oh, nothing.

752
00:52:20.596 --> 00:52:22.597
Uh, go back to sleep, honey.

753
00:52:22.681 --> 00:52:27.186
- You're obviously doing something.
- It's a... It's a surprise.

754
00:52:28.936 --> 00:52:30.313
That'll be the day.

755
00:52:33.983 --> 00:52:34.983
[sighs]

756
00:52:36.320 --> 00:52:39.322
- Are you all right, dear? You're shaking.
- Oh, I'm fine.

757
00:52:40.615 --> 00:52:43.159
You're not fine. You're shaking.

758
00:52:43.242 --> 00:52:44.702
Hey, listen,

759
00:52:44.786 --> 00:52:48.373
what do you say the four of us
go up to the cabin this weekend?

760
00:52:48.456 --> 00:52:49.641
We can spend the weekend up there.

761
00:52:49.666 --> 00:52:53.336
You can take the kids up there tomorrow,
and then get a head start on the clean-up.

762
00:52:53.420 --> 00:52:54.505
I see.

763
00:52:54.588 --> 00:52:55.963
You want to get rid of us

764
00:52:56.047 --> 00:52:58.925
so you can host
one of your big poker games.

765
00:52:59.009 --> 00:53:01.552
Uh, well, I guess you know me too well.

766
00:53:01.637 --> 00:53:02.929
[cries]

767
00:53:05.224 --> 00:53:08.434
Bradley, what's wrong?

768
00:53:10.019 --> 00:53:14.775
- What's happened?
- I don't know. I don't know.

769
00:53:14.858 --> 00:53:16.693
Forget it.

770
00:53:19.028 --> 00:53:21.907
I love you, that's all. And, uh...

771
00:53:23.742 --> 00:53:24.784
I wish...

772
00:53:27.371 --> 00:53:30.081
I could be a better husband to you.

773
00:53:30.164 --> 00:53:36.088
It's just a poker game, dear.
You don't have to feel so guilty.

774
00:53:37.588 --> 00:53:40.800
Sometimes, boys just need
to be with other boys.

775
00:54:11.331 --> 00:54:14.333
[footsteps approaching]

776
00:54:14.418 --> 00:54:17.128
- [Steph] You all right?
- I'm fine.

777
00:54:18.005 --> 00:54:20.798
- Big day today, huh?
- I suppose it is, yeah.

778
00:54:22.175 --> 00:54:23.469
I thought you'd be more excited.

779
00:54:25.012 --> 00:54:26.722
I don't know.

780
00:54:26.804 --> 00:54:29.682
When I was in prison, I told myself
that I'd be done with this life,

781
00:54:29.766 --> 00:54:31.768
get on the straight and narrow.

782
00:54:31.851 --> 00:54:34.438
Robbing banks
isn't exactly straight and narrow.

783
00:54:34.521 --> 00:54:36.648
Then why are you doing it?

784
00:54:38.942 --> 00:54:41.737
- That's a stupid fucking question.
- Why are you doing it?

785
00:54:43.362 --> 00:54:47.784
- For you.
- Bullshit. You're doing it for you.

786
00:54:49.411 --> 00:54:52.206
What are my options here, Steph, huh?

787
00:54:52.289 --> 00:54:56.251
Okay, we got no money.
We got no fucking opportunities.

788
00:54:57.543 --> 00:54:59.588
What are we supposed to do, huh?
You tell me, Steph.

789
00:54:59.670 --> 00:55:02.548
- What are we supposed to do?
- Nothing, I guess. I...

790
00:55:04.592 --> 00:55:07.471
I suppose this is just who you are.

791
00:55:10.891 --> 00:55:14.353
What the hell do you want from me, huh?

792
00:55:14.436 --> 00:55:17.563
For starters, you could accept
responsibility for my son's death.

793
00:55:17.648 --> 00:55:20.150
You are never gonna get over it, are you?

794
00:55:20.233 --> 00:55:23.987
Get over it? It's not a cold, Ed.

795
00:55:25.322 --> 00:55:29.159
- You don't think that I hurt, too?
- For what, eight months?

796
00:55:29.242 --> 00:55:33.329
I see! You wanted me to spend
ten years of my life in prison

797
00:55:33.413 --> 00:55:36.208
because of bad fucking luck?

798
00:55:36.291 --> 00:55:38.460
The school called us 'cause he was sick!

799
00:55:38.543 --> 00:55:41.170
He had a stomachache
and I'm the one who answered!

800
00:55:41.255 --> 00:55:44.048
- I was at work!
- So was I!

801
00:55:44.132 --> 00:55:47.802
At a drug lab! And you killed my son!

802
00:55:49.804 --> 00:55:52.474
You don't scare me, Ed.

803
00:55:52.557 --> 00:55:55.811
You only kill people by accident.

804
00:56:00.731 --> 00:56:03.985
[door opens, closes]

805
00:56:05.737 --> 00:56:07.947
Don't forget, Sally's got
her ballet recital tonight.

806
00:56:08.030 --> 00:56:09.030
Uh-huh.

807
00:56:09.907 --> 00:56:13.244
I want to get there an hour early
so I can get a good seat.

808
00:56:13.327 --> 00:56:14.746
That's great, sweetie.

809
00:56:15.831 --> 00:56:17.164
Wait, tonight? No, um...

810
00:56:18.916 --> 00:56:21.168
Sorry, I can't tonight.
I got a football reunion.

811
00:56:21.253 --> 00:56:23.255
You're gonna miss
your daughter's dance recital

812
00:56:23.338 --> 00:56:25.590
so you can drink beer
with a bunch of degenerates.

813
00:56:25.673 --> 00:56:26.757
Is your brother going, too?

814
00:56:26.842 --> 00:56:28.510
We asked him.
He's gotta work at the bank.

815
00:56:28.594 --> 00:56:30.554
Oh, well, if he can miss it,
then surely you can.

816
00:56:30.637 --> 00:56:32.197
You weren't even on the team
when they won.

817
00:56:32.222 --> 00:56:35.474
Okay, hey, sweetie. Hey! You know what?

818
00:56:35.559 --> 00:56:39.186
I'm so sorry I'm gonna miss
your thing tonight, but I have an idea.

819
00:56:39.271 --> 00:56:42.690
What about tomorrow you and me,
we go to Funland?

820
00:56:42.773 --> 00:56:44.025
She's got school tomorrow.

821
00:56:45.568 --> 00:56:48.614
You don't want to skip school
and spend the day with your dad?

822
00:56:48.697 --> 00:56:52.951
- Can Lissa come?
- [scoffs] No, Lissa can't come.

823
00:56:53.034 --> 00:56:57.623
- No, it's just you and me. That's the...
- Melissa is her imaginary friend.

824
00:56:59.583 --> 00:57:02.001
Oh! Lissa, yeah, sure. Bring her.

825
00:57:02.085 --> 00:57:05.838
Bring your whole imaginary
gang along. That's fine.

826
00:57:05.922 --> 00:57:08.175
Maybe we can go on Saturday.

827
00:57:08.257 --> 00:57:12.137
- There's no school...
- Damn it! What is the problem here?

828
00:57:12.219 --> 00:57:15.349
We are going to Funland tomorrow
and that's final!

829
00:57:17.224 --> 00:57:19.186
[sighs]
Are you happy now?

830
00:57:20.353 --> 00:57:22.271
- As a fucking clam!
- Oh...

831
00:57:29.112 --> 00:57:31.072
[vehicle approaching]

832
00:57:34.201 --> 00:57:35.242
Hey.

833
00:57:39.081 --> 00:57:40.539
Sorry, man.

834
00:57:41.416 --> 00:57:43.668
Escorting our state champion quarterback

835
00:57:43.751 --> 00:57:47.088
from his meeting
with our state champion parole officer.

836
00:57:47.172 --> 00:57:50.509
- Do you mind hoppin' in back?
- No, not at all.

837
00:57:50.592 --> 00:57:52.927
- Hey, Ed.
- How's it going, Reed?

838
00:57:53.010 --> 00:57:56.764
The back, huh?
Never been back here.

839
00:57:58.516 --> 00:58:00.811
- I have.
- [engine starts]

840
00:58:01.978 --> 00:58:06.358
My guess is... you don't wash it
after the canine unit uses it.

841
00:58:07.025 --> 00:58:08.902
You guys smell that?

842
00:58:08.985 --> 00:58:10.027
[laughs]

843
00:58:10.112 --> 00:58:12.614
No, no, no, it was, uh...

844
00:58:12.697 --> 00:58:16.034
- It was Westmoreland.
- Oh, yeah. Yes, yeah. Westmoreland.

845
00:58:16.117 --> 00:58:19.496
That was the game that Coach Denton called
Reed's goal line play on fourth and one,

846
00:58:19.579 --> 00:58:20.931
except we weren't on the goal line.

847
00:58:20.956 --> 00:58:22.057
Yeah, it was an important play.

848
00:58:22.081 --> 00:58:25.210
And I dropped back,
and I tossed a pretty little daisy

849
00:58:25.293 --> 00:58:27.628
- right in your waiting mitt.
- It was perfect.

850
00:58:27.713 --> 00:58:30.673
You were just so damn excited
to finally get your hands on the football,

851
00:58:30.757 --> 00:58:32.384
you forgot we were at midfield.

852
00:58:33.010 --> 00:58:34.719
And then, uh...
[laughing]

853
00:58:34.802 --> 00:58:37.639
And then, that big-ass linebacker, uh...

854
00:58:37.722 --> 00:58:39.391
- Reggie Cutler.
- Reggie Cutler.

855
00:58:39.474 --> 00:58:41.601
- Reggie Cutler.
- Fuck, that guy was big.

856
00:58:41.684 --> 00:58:44.938
- He just laid you out mid-jiggle.
- He was huge.

857
00:58:45.021 --> 00:58:46.231
[laughing]

858
00:58:46.313 --> 00:58:49.108
And then, 30 seconds later,
you stare up at me and you're like,

859
00:58:49.192 --> 00:58:50.818
"Uh, did we score?"

860
00:58:50.902 --> 00:58:52.862
And then you said...
You said, "Someone scored."

861
00:58:52.945 --> 00:58:54.614
[laughs]
Yeah, yeah. That's what you...

862
00:58:54.697 --> 00:58:58.034
Yeah, well, somebody scored,
but it sure as shit wasn't us.

863
00:58:58.117 --> 00:59:00.077
[chuckles]

864
00:59:00.161 --> 00:59:03.831
Still have that game on tape.
My dad shows it on Thanksgiving.

865
00:59:03.914 --> 00:59:05.625
[clears throat]

866
00:59:06.876 --> 00:59:08.461
Those were the days, huh?

867
00:59:29.106 --> 00:59:32.152
Come out here!
You got a phone call!

868
00:59:41.119 --> 00:59:43.079
- [Ed] <i>Hello?</i>
- [Dawkin] <i>It's me.</i>

869
00:59:43.163 --> 00:59:46.166
[Ed]
<i>Judge Dawkins. Lay it on me, brother.</i>

870
00:59:46.248 --> 00:59:49.585
You've got a lot of nerve blackmailing me
twice with the same tape.

871
00:59:49.668 --> 00:59:53.172
Yeah, I don't know.
It just kinda felt like a two-chit tape.

872
00:59:53.255 --> 00:59:56.342
You know, now, especially.
I hear you're running for the Senate.

873
00:59:56.425 --> 00:59:59.929
Burton, if you ever show up
flaunting this tape in my face again,

874
01:00:00.012 --> 01:00:01.306
I swear to God, I'm gonna...

875
01:00:01.389 --> 01:00:03.266
Relax, hombre, you think I'm gonna care,

876
01:00:03.349 --> 01:00:06.603
when I'm drinking pi? a coladas
on some deserted playa,

877
01:00:06.686 --> 01:00:08.730
about you and your 19-year-old
fucking butt-buddy?

878
01:00:08.813 --> 01:00:11.690
Oh, Jesus fuck!

879
01:00:11.775 --> 01:00:13.860
<i>Whenever you're ready
with those digits, Judge.</i>

880
01:00:19.240 --> 01:00:22.911
It's, uh... six, three times to the left,

881
01:00:22.994 --> 01:00:27.498
28, four times to the right,
86, three times to the left.

882
01:00:27.581 --> 01:00:30.918
Three times to the left. Got it.

883
01:00:31.920 --> 01:00:32.920
[hangs up]

884
01:00:39.469 --> 01:00:41.471
You can kickoff
whenever you're ready, man.

885
01:00:43.639 --> 01:00:45.474
You want me to take a shift tonight?

886
01:00:45.559 --> 01:00:49.186
Nah, nah. Bank duty is the sheriff's job.

887
01:00:50.146 --> 01:00:54.108
Dawkins will give me hell if it's not me
guarding his precious crop money.

888
01:00:54.192 --> 01:00:58.445
Plus, I don't want to ruin your night.
You seeing this mysterious Wendy again?

889
01:01:00.532 --> 01:01:03.909
Holy shit! You are.

890
01:01:04.744 --> 01:01:08.414
- Is it getting serious?
- No, it's just dinner.

891
01:01:09.833 --> 01:01:12.418
That's how it starts,
and then the next thing you know,

892
01:01:12.501 --> 01:01:14.420
little Wendys running
all around your house.

893
01:01:14.503 --> 01:01:15.503
Oh...

894
01:01:17.798 --> 01:01:19.550
I don't know, I don't know.

895
01:01:19.634 --> 01:01:21.052
- 602.
- 602.

896
01:01:21.135 --> 01:01:22.971
- Not 206.
- 602.

897
01:01:23.054 --> 01:01:25.306
- I got it!
- All right.

898
01:01:27.851 --> 01:01:28.851
[scoffs]

899
01:01:29.351 --> 01:01:31.730
What? It ain't like one drink
never killed nobody.

900
01:01:31.813 --> 01:01:36.067
Chris, we need every brain cell you've got
left in your head tonight, okay?

901
01:01:36.150 --> 01:01:38.695
Is... Is he making another stupid joke?

902
01:01:38.777 --> 01:01:41.572
- 'Cause I didn't get it!
- I'm not fucking around!

903
01:01:41.655 --> 01:01:43.992
- Hey, stop!
- Relax! Relax, okay?

904
01:01:44.074 --> 01:01:45.911
Everybody needs to chill the fuck out.

905
01:01:45.994 --> 01:01:48.871
That's what I'm trying to do.
This whole thing is freaking me out.

906
01:01:48.954 --> 01:01:52.291
Chris, Chris. Everything's gonna be fine.

907
01:01:52.375 --> 01:01:56.378
- Okay? Isn't that right, Andy?
- Five minutes. Easy in, easy out.

908
01:01:56.463 --> 01:01:57.983
You don't even have to leave your car.

909
01:01:58.005 --> 01:02:00.300
Yeah, well, why are we taking
my car anyway?

910
01:02:00.382 --> 01:02:02.469
Because everyone knows
I drive a bitchin' Camaro

911
01:02:02.552 --> 01:02:04.054
and Andy drives a gay-ass Porsche.

912
01:02:04.137 --> 01:02:06.199
No one has the slightest clue
as to what you drive. That's why.

913
01:02:06.222 --> 01:02:08.159
They probably think
that you don't even know how to drive.

914
01:02:08.182 --> 01:02:11.143
Of course, I fucking drive!
That's why I'm the goddamn driver.

915
01:02:11.228 --> 01:02:14.021
Yeah, and Andy's the lookout,
and I'm the one handling the safe.

916
01:02:14.105 --> 01:02:16.942
And if we all just do our jobs,
then everything will be perfectly fine.

917
01:02:17.025 --> 01:02:20.402
Look, he's right, Chris.
My brother doesn't even lock the door.

918
01:02:20.487 --> 01:02:22.697
I think he figures that the fact
that he's inside,

919
01:02:22.780 --> 01:02:25.074
no one is gonna try anything.
[chuckles]

920
01:02:25.157 --> 01:02:30.163
Seriously, he must be the stupidest cop
in the history of the police force.

921
01:02:30.246 --> 01:02:32.539
- Hey, Ed, can I talk to you a sec?
- Yeah.

922
01:02:33.583 --> 01:02:36.302
You know, you really shouldn't talk
about your own brother like that.

923
01:02:36.378 --> 01:02:38.338
Shut up. Just shut up.

924
01:02:40.047 --> 01:02:41.047
[clears throat]

925
01:02:41.090 --> 01:02:43.385
[Chris and Andy talking indistinctly]

926
01:02:43.467 --> 01:02:44.510
What's up?

927
01:02:46.137 --> 01:02:48.181
I'm sorry about what happened
this morning.

928
01:02:49.349 --> 01:02:50.516
Wow.
[chuckles]

929
01:02:50.599 --> 01:02:52.476
That's a new one.

930
01:02:52.559 --> 01:02:56.815
Listen, I've... I've been thinking
about what you said.

931
01:02:58.065 --> 01:03:00.943
About how you thought
you'd left this life behind.

932
01:03:02.070 --> 01:03:03.153
Did you mean that?

933
01:03:06.615 --> 01:03:07.867
Yeah.

934
01:03:07.951 --> 01:03:10.036
Then you should call this whole thing off.

935
01:03:10.119 --> 01:03:13.039
Call this whole thing... What do you mean?
This whole thing was your idea.

936
01:03:14.331 --> 01:03:17.626
Chris, Andy, Dawkins. You said
they'd all play ball and they fucking did.

937
01:03:19.003 --> 01:03:20.505
Ed, I'm serious.

938
01:03:21.922 --> 01:03:23.465
It's not too late.

939
01:03:27.679 --> 01:03:32.057
[clears throat]
Don't get skittish on me now, all right?

940
01:03:32.141 --> 01:03:34.601
We got this. Trust me.

941
01:03:34.686 --> 01:03:36.706
You're gonna be singing
a very different tune in a few hours

942
01:03:36.730 --> 01:03:38.940
when you're a very rich woman.

943
01:03:49.951 --> 01:03:52.077
All right, where were we, boys?

944
01:03:52.161 --> 01:03:53.579
[taps on table]

945
01:04:02.422 --> 01:04:07.217
[indistinct chatter]

946
01:04:09.094 --> 01:04:12.931
- Evening, fellas.
- Oh, Sheriff Sikes, my man!

947
01:04:13.016 --> 01:04:16.268
Listen, I can't tell you how grateful I am
that you're going to all this trouble

948
01:04:16.353 --> 01:04:17.644
to help us out once again.

949
01:04:17.728 --> 01:04:19.606
Really, it is no trouble at all.

950
01:04:19.688 --> 01:04:21.523
Great. Well, same procedure as usual.

951
01:04:21.608 --> 01:04:24.902
Uh, the cash will spend the night in here.
In the morning, we'll take it out,

952
01:04:24.985 --> 01:04:27.947
divvy it out to the other branches
to be paid out to the farmers

953
01:04:28.030 --> 01:04:29.490
when they come to cash their checks.

954
01:04:29.574 --> 01:04:32.327
That'll be going on for a few days.
Hold on one second.

955
01:04:33.994 --> 01:04:35.121
- There you go.
- Thank you.

956
01:04:35.204 --> 01:04:38.248
Thank you, my man. Thank you.

957
01:04:38.333 --> 01:04:43.713
So, uh, unless there's anything else,
I'm just gonna be heading home.

958
01:04:43.797 --> 01:04:46.965
I gotta get home
before Allison pitches a fit.

959
01:04:47.050 --> 01:04:50.302
I gotta be there
right when dinner is served.

960
01:04:50.387 --> 01:04:53.139
Judge, uh... you wanna...

961
01:04:54.264 --> 01:04:56.434
Oh! Yeah, sorry.

962
01:04:56.518 --> 01:04:58.103
[chuckles]

963
01:04:59.061 --> 01:05:02.315
Hey, listen, just as a point of curiosity,

964
01:05:02.398 --> 01:05:05.527
what would happen if someone
tried to rob this bank tonight?

965
01:05:05.610 --> 01:05:06.820
You'd shoot 'em, right?

966
01:05:08.153 --> 01:05:10.155
Well, that sort of depends
on the situation.

967
01:05:10.239 --> 01:05:14.786
Ideally, I'd like to arrest them
without resorting to violence.

968
01:05:14.869 --> 01:05:18.164
Well, shoot first, ask questions later.
That's what I always say.

969
01:05:19.456 --> 01:05:20.541
Know what I mean?

970
01:05:22.335 --> 01:05:24.711
Um, not really, no.

971
01:05:25.630 --> 01:05:32.010
Just know that if anything like that
were ever to happen,

972
01:05:32.094 --> 01:05:34.179
I'd have your back a hundred percent.

973
01:05:35.097 --> 01:05:38.351
I mean, no matter what the circumstances.

974
01:05:40.186 --> 01:05:41.827
That's awfully kind of you to say, Judge.

975
01:05:43.106 --> 01:05:47.277
Though, hopefully, tonight will just be
your typical quiet night at the bank.

976
01:05:48.862 --> 01:05:53.867
Of course. Okay. Well, I hope
you brought a crossword puzzle.

977
01:05:54.659 --> 01:05:55.659
[chuckles]

978
01:05:58.036 --> 01:06:00.581
Okay. Good-bye.

979
01:06:51.132 --> 01:06:52.509
[door squeaking open]

980
01:06:54.135 --> 01:06:55.385
[footsteps approaching]

981
01:06:56.137 --> 01:06:59.681
You move one muscle and I'll blow
your fucking brains all over the wall!

982
01:07:01.351 --> 01:07:03.228
Okay, get his gun.

983
01:07:04.394 --> 01:07:06.898
You... You get his gun. You get his...

984
01:07:06.981 --> 01:07:12.027
Fuck! You get the gun!
Okay. Now, go. Destroy it!

985
01:07:17.617 --> 01:07:19.452
- I can't!
- Cuff yourself!

986
01:07:19.536 --> 01:07:22.038
- Too high.
- What are you doing?

987
01:07:22.121 --> 01:07:26.918
What are you doing?
Smash it! Just smash it! Smash it!

988
01:07:29.336 --> 01:07:30.380
Smash it!

989
01:07:32.257 --> 01:07:34.800
- Smash it!
- I am!

990
01:07:34.884 --> 01:07:37.971
Smash it! What are you doing?

991
01:07:38.054 --> 01:07:39.222
Don't fucking move!

992
01:07:40.639 --> 01:07:45.978
Cut the wires! Cut the wires!
Just smash it! Smash it!

993
01:07:47.605 --> 01:07:52.443
Uh, yeah! Okay. Okay.

994
01:07:52.527 --> 01:07:54.362
Good! Now, go!

995
01:08:02.452 --> 01:08:05.914
Let me guess. Step two: unlock vault.

996
01:08:05.998 --> 01:08:08.960
Shut the fuck up!
Or I'll shoot you in the face!

997
01:08:11.086 --> 01:08:13.130
Hey, what's happening?

998
01:08:13.213 --> 01:08:15.967
What the fuck do you think is happening?
We're robbing a bank.

999
01:08:16.050 --> 01:08:17.885
I know, but inside, is it going good?

1000
01:08:19.429 --> 01:08:23.265
Yeah, Chris.
It's going real good. Super good.

1001
01:08:25.018 --> 01:08:26.060
Okay.

1002
01:08:40.574 --> 01:08:43.077
Fuck! Come on!

1003
01:08:43.161 --> 01:08:46.247
What is this,<i> The Price is Right</i>?
How many times you gonna spin that dial?

1004
01:08:46.331 --> 01:08:49.375
- Shut up or I'll shoot you...
- In the face. I get it, I get it.

1005
01:08:51.711 --> 01:08:54.631
- Do you mind if I finish my dinner?
- Will you just shut the fuck up?

1006
01:09:02.721 --> 01:09:04.056
Fuck!

1007
01:09:06.059 --> 01:09:09.895
What are you doing?
What are you doing? Get back!

1008
01:09:09.979 --> 01:09:11.689
- Just a second.
- Get back! Stay back!

1009
01:09:11.773 --> 01:09:13.149
Stay back! I'll shoot!

1010
01:09:13.231 --> 01:09:16.985
What are you...? Go back! Go back!
What are you doing?

1011
01:09:17.069 --> 01:09:19.905
What the fuck are you doing?
What are you...?

1012
01:09:19.988 --> 01:09:21.869
Let me see it.
You think I care about the money?

1013
01:09:21.948 --> 01:09:23.618
It's all federally insured anyway.

1014
01:09:23.701 --> 01:09:26.453
You...? You don't care
if I take the money?

1015
01:09:26.537 --> 01:09:31.000
- Easy, Ed, your accent's slippin'.
- I'm not Ed! I'm Doug!

1016
01:09:31.083 --> 01:09:35.962
Schwarzenegger!
Arnold's less successful... brother.

1017
01:09:36.046 --> 01:09:41.386
Fuck it! All right. Yeah, it's me!
I'm gonna be long gone,

1018
01:09:41.469 --> 01:09:44.639
anyway, by the time they get you
out of that fucking vault.

1019
01:09:44.721 --> 01:09:46.640
Huh? So, here. Good luck.

1020
01:09:51.938 --> 01:09:54.023
It's 86.

1021
01:09:57.359 --> 01:10:01.197
How do you read that
as a fucking eight, huh?

1022
01:10:01.279 --> 01:10:06.159
Six, 28, 86. It's his...
It's his fucking wedding anniversary.

1023
01:10:07.703 --> 01:10:09.788
[scoffs]
Yeah.

1024
01:10:11.498 --> 01:10:15.627
I can see it now with my...
with my mask off. Okay.

1025
01:10:23.010 --> 01:10:25.971
Yeah! Whoo!

1026
01:10:28.224 --> 01:10:30.851
Hey, Andy,
you think when this is all over,

1027
01:10:30.935 --> 01:10:32.979
things will go back
to the way they were before?

1028
01:10:33.770 --> 01:10:35.648
I sure as fuck hope not.

1029
01:10:35.731 --> 01:10:39.152
No, I mean, like, before everything.

1030
01:10:39.234 --> 01:10:41.028
Like, Ed Jr.

1031
01:10:44.114 --> 01:10:46.743
It'll never be like it was before Ed Jr.

1032
01:10:46.826 --> 01:10:52.832
Yeah. I guess people
really don't like dead kids, huh?

1033
01:10:52.914 --> 01:10:57.127
Yeah, no shit. They fucking love 'em.

1034
01:10:57.211 --> 01:10:59.796
We had some pretty good times
back in the day.

1035
01:10:59.881 --> 01:11:04.551
You and me. But now, 'cause of tonight...

1036
01:11:07.305 --> 01:11:08.765
I'll probably never see you again.

1037
01:11:11.057 --> 01:11:13.810
I guess that means
you're not planning on shootin' me.

1038
01:11:16.189 --> 01:11:20.234
Come on, Z, you think I'm actually capable
of doing something like that?

1039
01:11:20.318 --> 01:11:21.652
Jesus Christ.

1040
01:11:22.694 --> 01:11:26.698
I don't know.
You killed Ed Jr. pretty good.

1041
01:11:29.159 --> 01:11:31.496
[clears throat]
Excuse me?

1042
01:11:31.578 --> 01:11:33.413
You heard me.

1043
01:11:34.623 --> 01:11:39.753
- That was a fucking accident, Zeke.
- Hey, shit happens.

1044
01:11:43.716 --> 01:11:45.760
Fuck you, Zeke!

1045
01:11:45.842 --> 01:11:48.220
You sound like my goddamn wife.

1046
01:11:51.974 --> 01:11:53.768
Hey. Here.

1047
01:11:55.310 --> 01:11:58.523
Get in the fucking vault!
Get in the fucking vault, Zeke!

1048
01:12:00.149 --> 01:12:01.943
And if I suffocate in there
before morning,

1049
01:12:02.025 --> 01:12:05.029
I guess that'll be an accident too, right?

1050
01:12:05.112 --> 01:12:08.282
Do you want me to kill you?
'Cause I can fucking do that!

1051
01:12:08.365 --> 01:12:10.243
You know what they say...

1052
01:12:10.326 --> 01:12:12.828
"Once you take a life,
it's always easier the second time."

1053
01:12:17.416 --> 01:12:21.127
I could kill you.
I am on the edge right now.

1054
01:12:22.712 --> 01:12:24.923
I'll fucking do it!

1055
01:12:25.006 --> 01:12:30.095
Fuck! Do not fucking push me, Zeke!

1056
01:12:31.346 --> 01:12:32.849
Or what?

1057
01:12:33.640 --> 01:12:35.059
Or I'll...

1058
01:12:36.560 --> 01:12:39.104
[groaning, breathing heavily]

1059
01:12:44.277 --> 01:12:46.279
Oh, shit!

1060
01:12:47.572 --> 01:12:50.824
What the fuck?
What the fuck is happening, man?

1061
01:12:52.618 --> 01:12:53.953
What's happening?

1062
01:12:55.287 --> 01:12:57.539
You're robbing a bank, Ed.

1063
01:12:57.622 --> 01:13:00.251
And pretty soon, you're gonna shoot me,

1064
01:13:00.333 --> 01:13:02.295
and then race out that door
with the money.

1065
01:13:03.628 --> 01:13:06.006
But first, you'll kill Chris.
Maybe Dawkins.

1066
01:13:06.090 --> 01:13:08.985
But probably Chris, then Dawkins.
And once they're dead, you'll kill Andy.

1067
01:13:09.010 --> 01:13:10.261
What?

1068
01:13:10.344 --> 01:13:12.470
And then,
once all your loose ends are tied up,

1069
01:13:12.555 --> 01:13:15.234
you're gonna disappear with the money,
never to be heard from again.

1070
01:13:16.100 --> 01:13:19.729
Except... none of that's gonna happen

1071
01:13:19.811 --> 01:13:21.354
'cause I'm gonna kill you...

1072
01:13:21.439 --> 01:13:24.399
and I'm gonna bury you in a hole
out by Shimmer Lake.

1073
01:13:24.483 --> 01:13:29.238
What? Why are you doing this?
Why are you doing this, Zeke?

1074
01:13:29.779 --> 01:13:31.073
What the fuck?

1075
01:13:33.242 --> 01:13:37.537
Shit, what's happening?
What the fuck is going on?

1076
01:13:39.039 --> 01:13:42.376
- Justice, Ed.
- Justice... Justice for what?

1077
01:13:42.460 --> 01:13:45.171
We couldn't just let you get away with it.

1078
01:13:45.253 --> 01:13:49.382
Not you. Not Chris Morrow.
Not Andy Sikes.

1079
01:13:49.466 --> 01:13:51.176
Not Brad Dawkins.

1080
01:13:52.761 --> 01:13:56.140
He wasn't dead two weeks
and you were already cutting a deal.

1081
01:13:56.849 --> 01:13:58.768
You stole him from us.

1082
01:13:59.935 --> 01:14:01.686
You stole my baby.

1083
01:14:01.770 --> 01:14:04.564
Oh, come on. Come on.

1084
01:14:04.649 --> 01:14:07.652
He was my baby too, okay?

1085
01:14:08.985 --> 01:14:10.613
Don't you get it?

1086
01:14:13.990 --> 01:14:16.159
He wasn't your baby.

1087
01:14:16.243 --> 01:14:19.372
What are you talking about?
Stop saying that.

1088
01:14:19.454 --> 01:14:20.664
Ed...

1089
01:14:25.670 --> 01:14:29.631
Do you remember
back when we were all so close?

1090
01:14:31.466 --> 01:14:33.511
Steph and I made a mistake.

1091
01:14:34.636 --> 01:14:35.637
No.

1092
01:14:37.139 --> 01:14:39.850
I stayed with you
because I still loved you.

1093
01:14:41.476 --> 01:14:45.981
And I hoped seeing that beautiful boy
could have straightened us out,

1094
01:14:46.064 --> 01:14:48.359
could have... could have saved us.

1095
01:14:49.694 --> 01:14:51.569
Then you killed him.

1096
01:14:53.989 --> 01:14:55.699
It was an accident.

1097
01:14:58.411 --> 01:15:00.246
It was an accident.

1098
01:15:03.748 --> 01:15:04.750
Zeke...

1099
01:15:04.833 --> 01:15:07.420
We thought we were doing the right thing.

1100
01:15:08.712 --> 01:15:09.963
We thought you'd changed.

1101
01:15:12.382 --> 01:15:14.385
He was my son, Ed.

1102
01:15:26.479 --> 01:15:27.814
I'm sorry.

1103
01:15:27.898 --> 01:15:29.692
Yeah...

1104
01:15:31.234 --> 01:15:32.235
I'm sorry, too.

1105
01:15:38.408 --> 01:15:39.577
I'm going in.

1106
01:15:39.659 --> 01:15:41.287
- The fuck you are!
- I'm going in there!

1107
01:15:41.369 --> 01:15:43.372
No! No, Chris, you're the driver.

1108
01:15:43.456 --> 01:15:45.141
You get back in the driver's seat
right now.

1109
01:15:45.166 --> 01:15:47.208
For all we know,
those could've been warning shots.

1110
01:15:47.292 --> 01:15:48.918
- Warning shots?
- Yes.

1111
01:15:49.002 --> 01:15:51.005
- What the fuck?
- No, Chris! No!

1112
01:15:54.050 --> 01:15:55.301
[exhales]

1113
01:16:01.890 --> 01:16:04.518
- This is really happening, isn't it?
- Yes.

1114
01:16:05.560 --> 01:16:08.689
- Zeke, this is really happening.
- Yes.

1115
01:16:09.939 --> 01:16:13.152
Okay. Are you ready?

1116
01:16:14.069 --> 01:16:15.820
Here.

1117
01:16:21.284 --> 01:16:23.912
Relax. Breathe.

1118
01:16:29.376 --> 01:16:32.003
- Does it hurt?
- No, I don't feel a thing.

1119
01:16:32.087 --> 01:16:36.050
All right, give me the pistol
and get the tarp.

1120
01:16:41.012 --> 01:16:43.765
Oh, shit! Fuck! Go!

1121
01:16:43.849 --> 01:16:45.768
Fuck! Fuck! Fuck! Fuck!

1122
01:16:45.850 --> 01:16:49.063
Fuck! Chris, fuck, it's Zeke!
Go, go, go, go, go!

1123
01:16:49.145 --> 01:16:50.480
[tires screeching]

1124
01:17:29.435 --> 01:17:30.813
[starts engine]

1125
01:18:17.818 --> 01:18:20.112
[alarm ringing]

1126
01:18:33.583 --> 01:18:35.961
- Why? Why?
- [stammering] I'm sorry, Andy.

1127
01:18:36.045 --> 01:18:38.296
- I fucked up.
- [vehicle door opens]

1128
01:18:38.380 --> 01:18:40.423
Oh, fuck. We're fucked, Andy.

1129
01:18:40.506 --> 01:18:42.027
- We're fucked.
- [vehicle door closes]

1130
01:18:45.511 --> 01:18:46.596
License and registration.

1131
01:18:46.680 --> 01:18:49.182
- [tires squealing]
- [alarm ringing]

1132
01:18:55.314 --> 01:18:57.690
- Zeke?
- Back here!

1133
01:18:59.859 --> 01:19:00.860
Oh, shit!

1134
01:19:00.944 --> 01:19:02.363
[engine running]

1135
01:19:05.240 --> 01:19:06.408
[engine stops]

1136
01:19:06.492 --> 01:19:08.577
- [Steph grunting]
- [banging]

1137
01:19:16.252 --> 01:19:17.795
[man on police radio]
<i>019. Come in.</i>

1138
01:19:17.877 --> 01:19:20.756
- Shit! Oh, shit! Fuck!
- [officer] This is 019.

1139
01:19:20.838 --> 01:19:24.051
<i>We got an alarm signal
coming from First Mackey Bank.</i>

1140
01:19:25.386 --> 01:19:29.515
- I'm gonna shoot him.
- What? No! Get the... You stupid...

1141
01:19:29.597 --> 01:19:31.015
[officer]
Chris Morrow...

1142
01:19:33.560 --> 01:19:37.355
- It's your lucky day.
- Really?

1143
01:19:37.439 --> 01:19:39.899
- Ed Burton shot you?
- Yeah.

1144
01:19:39.984 --> 01:19:42.110
Ed shot me.

1145
01:19:42.194 --> 01:19:44.070
Then he took off out back with the money,

1146
01:19:44.154 --> 01:19:47.573
and two others took off out front
in a blue Caddy.

1147
01:19:47.658 --> 01:19:50.327
I took some shots at 'em,
but I just got too woozy.

1148
01:19:50.411 --> 01:19:52.453
I had to come back in and lie down.

1149
01:19:52.537 --> 01:19:56.041
Hi, I need an ambulance and, uh, cops.
I need... I need a lot of cops.

1150
01:20:03.172 --> 01:20:04.173
[grunts]

1151
01:20:07.552 --> 01:20:09.989
It's just something to numb the pain
before we take you to the hospital.

1152
01:20:10.014 --> 01:20:13.766
- No, no, I can't. I'm allergic.
- You have to have something.

1153
01:20:13.850 --> 01:20:15.435
Trust me, I'll be fine.

1154
01:20:16.561 --> 01:20:18.162
[Reed]
He says it was Ed Burton for sure.

1155
01:20:18.188 --> 01:20:22.943
He couldn't make out any other faces.
He did say they sped off in a blue Caddy.

1156
01:20:25.029 --> 01:20:26.279
What?

1157
01:20:35.122 --> 01:20:36.289
Thank you.

1158
01:20:41.337 --> 01:20:44.088
- What's going on?
- Um...

1159
01:20:44.172 --> 01:20:45.613
I was just talking to Pete and Luke,

1160
01:20:45.631 --> 01:20:50.179
and not five minutes ago, they pulled
over a Caddy for excessive speeding.

1161
01:20:51.055 --> 01:20:52.180
And?

1162
01:20:53.890 --> 01:20:55.225
It was your brother.

1163
01:21:10.032 --> 01:21:15.119
- Man, Zeke. This is a real mess.
- Yeah, it's an old mess.

1164
01:21:15.203 --> 01:21:16.997
How do you mean?

1165
01:21:17.081 --> 01:21:23.170
I mean, this is what happens
when wrongs go un-righted. They fester.

1166
01:21:23.252 --> 01:21:24.880
You talking about Ed Jr.?

1167
01:21:24.962 --> 01:21:28.759
Yeah, you're damn fucking right
I'm talking about Ed Jr.

1168
01:21:28.841 --> 01:21:31.677
Eight lousy months he got.

1169
01:21:31.761 --> 01:21:34.042
Don't worry about it. We'll get him.
http://archiveha.org/

1170
01:21:35.181 --> 01:21:36.725
I'm not worried about it, Reed.

1171
01:21:38.810 --> 01:21:40.561
As far as I'm concerned...

1172
01:21:42.480 --> 01:21:44.001
he's already got.
http://archiveha.org/
